{"id":1,"lang":"zh","text":"这个概念,在此涵盖所有声乐品种中区别于\"唱\"的,与 言 语 之\"说\"发 声 形 态 接近的音声,如各种\"说\"\"白\"\"诵\"\"吟\"以 及 唱段中夹杂 的 与 言 语(语言行为在语言界术语中谓 之\"言 语\")中 的\"说\"类 似 的 音 声(音符无法准确捕捉的声乐音声).","cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27]","en_tr":"This concept covers all vocal sounds that differ from strict \"singing\" due to being recitative in style, such as various \"shūo說,\" \"bái白,\" \"sòng誦,\" \"yīng吟\" and other speaking sounds (which staff notation cannot accurately label) in vocal passages.","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27] (See also 乐说 yuèshuō)","term":"吟 yín"}
{"id":2,"lang":"zh","text":"如果我們把我們的靈界當作是我們的上界,那末,我們亦可以把音樂當作是上界的語言.\" Li (2024) [1.17]. \"凡屬人類,至少都具有幾分的音樂性,所以我們亦可以把音樂當作是靈界的一種世界語言…或者不可以得到相當的了解,但是所謂音樂是靈界的世界語言云云,是指那些差不多有同一的文化程度的人們來說.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.18]","en_tr":"If we consider our spiritual world our upper realm (shangjie), we can also understand Music as a language of the upper realm.\" Li (2024) [1.17]. \"Consequently, we can perceive Music as a world language of the upper realm…when I refer to Music as the world language of the upper realm, I am addressing those who possess a similar level of literacy.","en_cite":"(For more on music literacy and the upper realm, see Li (2024) [1.18]. For more on the upper realm, see Li (2024) Introduction","term":"上界 shàng jìe"}
{"id":3,"lang":"zh","text":"因為在文人看來,道是造分天地,化成萬物的一樣東西,凡屬可以行道的詩書易禮,都是道的工具,固不僅音樂是如是。你們要把音樂的獨立生命奪回來,自然要把「樂是禮的附庸」之說打破,即是要把「音樂是道的一種工具」之說打破,必要把這一類的學說打破,然後音樂的獨立生命綫有着落.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.5]","en_tr":"For the literati, the Way generated Heaven, the Earth, and ten thousand things (wanwu). Like Music—Poetry, Literature, and Ritual were means for the literati to unite with the Way. If you wish to retrieve the lost autonomy of Music, you must not only dismiss the idea that Music is a subsidiary of Ritual, but also dismantle such kind of thought as Music is an instrument of the Way.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.5]","term":"道 dào"}
{"id":4,"lang":"zh","text":"因為在包辦音樂的文人看來,音樂是應該受聲韻的支配,祇要那些詞句是和聲韻沒有違背,自可以依照同一樣受聲韻支配的音樂把他唱出來.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.5]","en_tr":"For the monopolizing literati understood that Music was governed by tone patterns. As long as the words and tone patterns harmonized, they could be sung with the same melody.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.5]","term":"声韵 shēngyùn "}
{"id":5,"lang":"zh","text":"这个概念,在此涵盖所有声乐品种中区别于\"唱\"的,与 言 语 之\"说\"发 声 形 态 接近的音声,如各种\"说\"\"白\"\"诵\"\"吟\"以 及 唱段中夹杂 的 与 言 语(语言行为在语言界术语中谓 之\"言 语\")中 的\"说\"类 似 的 音 声(音符无法准确捕捉的声乐音声).","cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27]","en_tr":"This concept covers all vocal sounds that differ from strict \"singing\" due to being recitative in style, such as various \"shūo說,\" \"bái白,\" \"sòng誦,\" \"yīng吟\" and other speaking sounds (which staff notation cannot accurately label) in vocal passages.","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27](See also 乐说 yuèshuō)","term":"诵/誦 sòng"}
{"id":6,"lang":"zh","text":"人們曉得創造成一定的音的法律,又曉得根據這些音的法律創造成一個個的樂音,所以我們除承認人們對於自然界是處於立法者的地位之外,還要承認所謂音樂云云,都是建築在虛偽的根基上面,因為祇根據自己定出來的法律,創造成一些藝術,偏又要說牠是盡真,盡善,盡美.","cite":"Li (2024) [2.7]","en_tr":"Humans understand how to enact certain musical laws, and to create musical tones according to these laws. Therefore not only should we acknowledge humans as legislators against nature, but we should also acknowledge that music, conceived in broad terms, are built upon the basis of Pretense. For humans create art based on self-established laws, while claiming that art embodies truth, perfection, and beauty.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [2.7]","term":"法律 fǎlǜ"}
{"id":7,"lang":"zh","text":"中國舊日的文人是包辦一切的,祇有文人才配稱儒者。他們當日竟提出那個「一事不知,儒者之恥」的口號,儒冠的文人要把音樂圈入他的勢力範圍裏面,這自然是很難怪了。。。因為在文人看來,道是造分天地,化成萬物的一樣東西,凡屬可以行道的詩書易禮,都是道的工具,固不僅音樂是如是。","cite":"Li (2024)","en_tr":"The literati in ancient China monopolized everything; only they were considered worthy of being called Confucians. They proposed that \"ignorance of any matter brings shame upon a Confucian,\" in order to expand their sphere of influence to the realm of Music […] For the literati, the Way generated Heaven, the Earth, and ten thousand things (wanwu). Like Music—Poetry, Literature, and Ritual were means for the literati to unite with the Way.","en_cite":"Li (2024)","term":"文人 wén rén"}
{"id":8,"lang":"zh","text":"這樣離不開舞的音樂,因為實際上不過是禮的附庸,所以我們不能夠把牠當作是一種獨立的藝術。你們承認音樂是一種獨立的藝術,那末,你們便不能夠把牠當作是禮的附庸。","cite":"Li (2024) [1.17]","en_tr":"If we consider our spiritual world our upper realm (shangjie), we can also understand Music as a language of the upper realm.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.17] (See also: 上界 shàng jìe)","term":"音乐 yīn yuè"}
{"id":9,"lang":"zh","text":"你們承認音樂是一種獨立的藝術,那末,你們便不能夠把牠當作是禮的附庸.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]","en_tr":"Since Music, in this sense, was but a subsidiary of Ritual, we cannot consider it to be an autonomous art. If you consider Music to be an autonomous art, you cannot consider it to be a subsidiary of Ritual.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.4] (See also: 礼 lǐ)","term":"音乐 yīn yuè"}
{"id":10,"lang":"zh","text":"五個音牠的職守無非是要那一般樂工平時練熟宮商角徵羽那五個音.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]","en_tr":"The duty of the Music Ministry was to ensure that the musicians mastered the five tones—gong, shang, jue, zhi, and yu.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]","term":"五(个)音 wǔ (gè) yīn"}
{"id":11,"lang":"zh","text":"自複音音樂得到最美滿的發達以來,無論那一度音程,亦無論那一種聲調,都可以憑著和音的使用.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.12]","en_tr":"Since the consummate development of polyphonic music, the use of harmony has had the capability to alter the nature of any interval or mode.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.12]","term":"音程 yīn chéng"}
{"id":12,"lang":"zh","text":"不論怎麼樣的一個樂音,誰也未曾在自然界裏面聽過。牠那種有一定的數目可查的顫動,以及牠的音色,都是由人們創造出來的,並不是從自然界照樣學來的。","cite":"Li (2024) [2.7] (See: 音 yīn, 声 shēng)","en_tr":"No musical tones can be heard in nature. They are scrutable vibrations; their timbre is manufactured by humans, not emulated from nature.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [2.7]","term":"音色 yīnsè"}
{"id":13,"lang":"zh","text":"这个概念,在此涵盖所有声乐品种中区别于\"唱\"的,与 言 语 之\"说\"发 声 形 态 接近的音声,如各种\"说\"\"白\"\"诵\"\"吟\"以 及 唱段中夹杂 的 与 言 语(语言行为在语言界术语中谓 之\"言 语\")中 的\"说\"类 似 的 音 声(音符无法准确捕捉的声乐音声).","cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27]","en_tr":"This concept covers all vocal sounds that differ from strict \"singing\" due to being recitative in style, such as various \"shūo說,\" \"bái白,\" \"sòng誦,\" \"yīng吟\" and other speaking sounds (which staff notation cannot accurately label) in vocal passages.","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27] (See also 乐说 yuèshuō)","term":"白bái"}
{"id":14,"lang":"zh","text":"所谓\"乐 说\",实指中国传统声乐品 种 中的\"说\"...这个概念,在此涵盖所有声乐品种中 区别于\"唱\"的,与 言 语 之\"说\"发 声 形 态 接近的音声,如各种\"说\"\"白\"\"诵\"\"吟\"以 及唱段中夹杂 的 与 言 语(语言行为在语言界 术语中谓 之\"言 语\")中 的\"说\"类 似 的 音 声(音符无法准确捕捉的声乐音声).","cite":"(Qian (2024) [1.27])","en_tr":"\"Yuèshuō樂說\" (literally \"musical speech\") refers to speaking within traditional Chinese vocal musics. […] This concept covers all vocal sounds that differ from strict \"singing\" due to being recitative in style, such as various \"shūo說,\" \"bái白,\" \"sòng誦,\" \"yīng吟\" and other speaking sounds (which staff notation cannot accurately label) in vocal passages.","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27]","term":"乐说 yuèshuō"}
{"id":15,"lang":"zh","text":"因為樂不過是禮的附庸,所謂先王以作樂崇德,就是要用崇德的樂完成禮的全體大用.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]","en_tr":"The former kings made Music to ennoble the Virtue (de), for they would like to use such ennobling Music to fulfill the comprehensive purpose of Ritual.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]. A related concept: see Li (2024) Footnote 11, \"mingde 明德 (the realizing or summoning of virtue)\"","term":"德 dé"}
{"id":16,"lang":"zh","text":"我們這裏姑就人類來說,凡屬人類,不問他是到了怎麼樣的文化程度,遇着說出來的話不能夠滿足他的內界要求的時候,他總會由自己的內界發出一些聲響來,或歡笑,或愁歎,這些由人們的內界發出來的自然的聲響,就是音樂的原素。音樂是用來補救說話的缺乏的一種語言,這就是希臘人對於音樂的根本理解.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.16]","en_tr":"However civilized a human being is, when confronted with speech that fails to satisfy the demands of their inner realm (neijie), it will inevitably produce sounds—be they joyful or sorrowful—that arise from within. These natural sounds from the inner realm are the sources of Music. Music is a language that compensates for the limitations of speech. This fundamental understanding of Music constituted the core belief held by the Greeks.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.16]. For more commentary on the inner realm, see Li (2024) [2.1, 2.6, 2.10, 2.12, 2.15] and Footnote 23","term":"内界 nèi jìe"}
{"id":17,"lang":"zh","text":"我說要向西方乞靈,這亦是很容易喚起,何消你說這一類的答話。\" Li (2024). \"西方的學者們對於音樂的研究,雖然是有許多獨到的地方,但是,因為各人的見解不同,所以你亦很不容易認定某一派的學說是對,某一派的學說是不對,因為不論那一派的學說,牠都是帶有一部分的真理,但是同時卻亦有許多不對的地方,你要把各派學說的短長略爲論列一下,恐怕既經要佔滿了這本小冊子的篇幅,所以我這裏祇好把那兩派各走極端的學說先拿來大略說一說。","cite":"Li (2024)","en_tr":"Tsing Chu (1934a) critiqued the contemporaneous view that the import of Western music into China was a form of cultural imperialism, and suggested that the Chinese should study Western music as a means of reforming [gaige] and/or improving [gailiang] national music. Elsewhere he had elaborated on concrete ways of reforming and/or improving national music in terms of scale, instrument, vocal techniques, and love (1931a, 1–11); see also Li 1930, 36–8. On the discussion of national music during Li's time, see, for example, Zheng 1928; Xiao 1939.","en_cite":"Li (2024)","term":"西方 xī fāng"}
{"id":18,"lang":"zh","text":"中國人向來是樂與詩書禮並重的,像禮樂治天下這一類的話,舊日中國人亦不知道說了多少 […] 便把那些叫做什麼始平之章,景平之章,咸平之章,壽平之章,嘉平之章,永平之章,熙平之章,清平之章,太平之章,祐平之章,以及別的什麼平之章歌奏起來,又佐以什麼干羽之舞.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]","en_tr":"For the Chinese, Music has always been considered on an equal footing with Poetry (shi), Literature (shu), and Ritual (li), as evident in such stale expressions as \"Ritual and Music rule the Heaven and the Earth […] Musicians and dancers could play and dance according to various ritual contexts like Shiping, Jingping, Xianping, Shouping, Jiaping, Yongping, Xiping, Qingping, Taiping, Youping, and so forth.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.4]","term":"礼 lǐ"}
{"id":19,"lang":"zh","text":"仍然是站在地域性声乐研究的角度,我提出,至少有五个研究范畴,…1.\"乡韵\"溯源;","cite":"(Qian (2024) [1.21-22])","en_tr":"Taking again the perspective of regional vocal music research, I have proposed that there are at least five aspects to this research. […] (1) Tracing the source of \"xiangyun鄉韻\" (regional musical charm)…","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.21-22]","term":"乡韵 xiāngyùn "}
{"id":20,"lang":"zh","text":"比方你要創作一首樂歌,當你看見那首歌文的時候,你既然被那首歌文的聲韻限死那末,你那裏還能夠作曲?你就勉強做出一篇樂歌來,你這種工作,亦祇可以說是填曲,決不可以說是作曲.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.5]","en_tr":"Consider composing a song: If you restrict yourself to the tone patterns of the lyrics, how can you truly create? Even if you manage to compose, the result may seem forced and strained; it would not be a composition, but an exercise of fitting music into words.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.5]","term":"乐歌/樂歌 yuègē"}
{"id":21,"lang":"zh","text":"因為既已說是樂音,自然不是自然界的音。不論怎麼樣的一個樂音,誰也未曾在自然界裏面聽過。牠那種有一定的數目可查的顫動,以及牠的音色,都是由人們創造出來的,並不是從自然界照樣學來的。人們曉得創造成一定的音的法律,又曉得根據這些音的法律創造成一個個的樂音,所以我們除承認人們對於自然界是處於立法者的地位之外,還要承認所謂音樂云云,都是建築在虛偽的根基上面,因為祇根據自己定出來的法律,創造成一些藝術,偏又要說牠是盡真,盡善,盡美,這樣沒有自然界的根據的創造,不是虛偽是什麼?","cite":"Li (2024) [2.7]","en_tr":"For musical tones, as the term itself suggests, are not the sounds of nature. No musical tones can be heard in nature. They are scrutable vibrations; their timbre is manufactured by humans, not emulated from nature. Humans understand how to enact certain musical laws, and to create musical tones according to these laws. Therefore not only should we acknowledge humans as legislators against nature, but we should also acknowledge that music, conceived in broad terms, are built upon the basis of Pretense. For humans create art based on self-established laws, while claiming that art embodies truth, perfection, and beauty. How can this unnatural creation not a Pretense?","en_cite":"Li (2024) [2.7]","term":"自然界 zìránjiè"}
{"id":22,"lang":"zh","text":"中國舊日的詞,首首都是可以拿來唱的。怎樣唱?就是有了一個詞牌的音樂之後,你便可以填上一些詞句,不計這些詞句是雄壯,抑或衰澀,是歡樂,抑或愁苦,你都可以依照同一樣的音樂把牠唱出來。","cite":"Li (2024) (See also: 词牌 cí pái)","en_tr":"Every lyric poetry (ci) in ancient China could be sung. How? Once the tunes (cipai) were set, one could fill it out with lines and words in accordance with the tone patterns.","en_cite":"Li (2024)","term":"词 cí"}
{"id":23,"lang":"zh","text":"这个概念,在此涵盖所有声乐品种中区别于\"唱\"的,与 言 语 之\"说\"发 声 形 态 接近的音声,如各种\"说\"\"白\"\"诵\"\"吟\"以 及 唱段中夹杂 的 与 言 语(语言行为在语言界术语中谓 之\"言 语\")中 的\"说\"类 似 的 音 声(音符无法准确捕捉的声乐音声).","cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27]","en_tr":"This concept covers all vocal sounds that differ from strict \"singing\" due to being recitative in style, such as various \"shūo說,\" \"bái白,\" \"sòng誦,\" \"yīng吟\" and other speaking sounds (which staff notation cannot accurately label) in vocal passages.","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.27] (See also 乐说 yuèshuō)","term":"說 shūo"}
{"id":24,"lang":"zh","text":"希臘人曾定下了許多的音樂法則,雖然就當日的單音音樂來說,不論那一個法則都是持之有故,言之成理,但是應用到現時的複音音樂,大都是沒有多大的用處,就祇把牠應用到區區的曲調上面,亦是用不着。","cite":"Li (2024)","en_tr":"\"The Greeks established numerous musical principles which, in the context of their monophonic music, were logical and well-founded. Yet, when applied to contemporary polyphonic music, most of these principles lose their relevance.'","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.13]","term":"单音音乐/單音音樂 dānyīn yīnyuè"}
{"id":25,"lang":"zh","text":"我這裏祇說各個音類,(即世人所謂音調,如C調,G調之類,)希臘人對於各個音類,認為是各有各的特性,決不可以把牠混淆.","cite":"Li (2024) [1.12]","en_tr":"Here I shall only discuss the different categories of tunes (referred to by earthly beings as \"modes,\" such as C major, G major, etc.). The Ancient Greeks believed that each mode has its own character, and should not be mixed up. Some music theory books nowadays still attempt to preserve this understanding of mode characters and apply it to contemporary music.","en_cite":"Li (2024) [1.12]","term":"音调 yīndiào"}
{"id":26,"lang":"zh","text":"上有 音 符,下 有 音 标,只 用 于 声 乐 作品,故称\"双音唱谱\"…因此使用\"双音唱谱\"不仅能使非拼音文字的唱词 展 示 唱 词 的 音 声,还 能 让 唱 腔与唱词都具备通用的音响符号.","cite":"(Qian (2024) [1.24-25])","en_tr":"I refer to this type of score as \"shuāngyīn Vocal Notation雙音唱譜 (Double-Tone Notation),\" which includes both musical notes and words plus IPA […] Therefore, using shuāngyīn Vocal Notation not only allows the sounds of chàngcí to be notated for non-phonetic scripts, but also puts both the chàngqīang and the chàngcí in the form of a universally recognized symbolic system.","en_cite":"Qian (2024) [1.24-25]","term":"双音 shuāngyīn"}
{"id":27,"lang":"ja","text":"し 具 体 的 に お 聞 き し た い の で す が 、 た とえ ば 、 先 ⽣ は 韓 国 の 雅 楽 か ら 何 か 受 け られ た 影 響 は ご ざ い ま す か 。 私 は 先 ⽣ の 作 品 に そ れ を 感 じ る の で す が \" … \"全 く そ の 通 り で す 。 ⽇ 本 の 雅 楽 は 韓 国 か ら 伝 来 し た 部 分 と 中 国 か ら 伝 来 し た 部 分 が あ り 、 韓 国 の 雅 楽 と は 内 容 的 に 少し 質 が 違 い ま す .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese,51)","en_tr":"For example, have you been influenced by Korean A-ak [Korean ceremonial court music]? I can sense its influence in your pieces. . .\" \"Exactly as you said. Japanese court music has parts that are imported from Korea and parts that are from China. But its contents are qualitatively different from Korean A-ak.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"韓国の雅楽 Kankoku no gagaku"}
{"id":28,"lang":"ja","text":"日本の作曲家たちは、従来、作曲のマテリアルは、現代でも古い西洋の伝統的な形式観に何かしら沿っているのではないでしょうか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"Perhaps Japanese composers follow the old Western traditional formalism even though the compositional materials [マテリアル] might be modern.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"形式観 keishiki-kan"}
{"id":29,"lang":"ja","text":"私の音楽はモニスティッシュです。というのは、私の音楽は複音楽的じゃないし、多応的な音楽ではありません。たとえばアロイス・ツインマーマン、彼のは多元的な音楽ですね。根源が違っている音楽的な要素が同時に流れて秩序を保ちつつ、対立しながら、ついにはそれらが和合して、皆楽的な大きな向上をするというものです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 52)","en_tr":"My music is monistic (monistisch). My music is not polyphonic or pluralistic. For example, Bernd Alois Zimmermann's music is pluralistic. Elements from different roots flow together, maintain order, oppose, but ultimately come together to greatly elevate the music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.1])","term":"モニスティmonisuti"}
{"id":30,"lang":"ja","text":"私の音楽はモニスティッシュです。というのは、私の音楽は複音楽的じゃないし、多応的な音楽ではありません。たとえばアロイス・ツインマーマン、彼のは多元的な音楽ですね。根源が違っている音楽的な要素が同時に流れて秩序を保ちつつ、対立しながら、ついにはそれらが和合して、皆楽的な大きな向上をするというものです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 52)","en_tr":"My music is monistic (monistisch). My music is not polyphonic or pluralistic. For example, Bernd Alois Zimmermann's music is pluralistic. Elements from different roots flow together, maintain order, oppose, but ultimately come together to greatly elevate the music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.1])","term":"複音楽 fuku ongaku"}
{"id":31,"lang":"ja","text":"さてAでは上段が下段に比較して細かい分割を行っているが、この両者の関係はかならずしも一概に決定し難く、ある一方の終止音が支配的である旋律中に、他の終止音が終止音としての意味を持たず、単に経過的に現れることも多く、また4度とか5度は、純粋にその音域を制限するものではなく、その上下に随時経過音が付加されうる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 2]","en_tr":"For now, in A, I have made narrower divisions in the upper analysis than in the lower, but the relation between the two is certainly hard to determine as a rule. On the other hand, for the part of the melody controlled by one of the ending notes, the other ending note does not function as the ending note but simply appears in passing [passing tone]. Also, fourths and fifths may not purely limit the range of notes, and extra notes might be added above or below.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.2, brackets added separately]","term":"経過音 keika oto"}
{"id":32,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4].","term":"自由な音語 jiyūna otogo"}
{"id":33,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 今 度 は 器 楽 曲 に 移 り ま し て 、 す べ て の 器 楽 曲 は ま ず 声 楽 から 受 け 継 い で 、 そ れ を 発 展 さ せ た も の とい っ て も い い わ け で す 。 た と え ば 「 ⽝ 等 」と い い ま し て 、 横 笛 を ⾧ く し た 形 の 韓 国 の 民 族 楽 器 が あ り ま し て 、 そ れ で 奏 さ れ る 節 回 し は 歌 唱 を 受 け 継 い だ も の で す 。そ し て 、 そ こ に は 線 的 な ⾳ 楽 の 妙 味 が ある わ け で す.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"And it also expands to instrumental music. One could say that all instrumental music is developed by continuing ideas from vocal music. For example, a flute-like instrument made with bamboo [橫笛] called Dae-gum is one of the Korean traditional instruments. Melodies played by that instrument are inherited from singing. They have their own charm of linear music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.5])","term":"橫笛 yoko fue"}
{"id":34,"lang":"ja","text":"先生が獄中で書かれたオペラのことですが、先生は健康も害されて、その オペラ自体は演奏される見通しすらない し、その作品自体が獄中から出れるかど うかもわからない、そういった中で、意 識を超越して一気にお書きになったとう かがったのですが。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 59]","en_tr":"Regarding the opera you had composed while in prison [Die Witwe des Schmetterlings (Butterfly Widow)], at the time, you were in poor health, there was no perspective for its performance, and you weren't even sure whether you could transport the score outside of the prison cell. How were you able to overcome senses [意識] and compose in these circumstances with one stroke?","en_cite":"Park (2024) [6.1]","term":"オペラ opera"}
{"id":35,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"オペラ opera"}
{"id":36,"lang":"ja","text":"核音の周辺の音は、結局核音からあまり簡単に飛躍しないところから見ると、この核音に従属する性質を持つと思える。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 6]","en_tr":"When we see that the notes around a nuclear tone do not easily leap from the nuclear tone, we can hypothesize that their nature is subordinate to the nuclear tone.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3]","term":"音 oto"}
{"id":37,"lang":"ja","text":"それは仏教的な哲学です。全くの無から何かの音が生まれるんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 56-57]","en_tr":"From a complete void, some tones emerge. It is by coincidence.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.2]","term":"音 oto"}
{"id":38,"lang":"ja","text":"流 れ る 線 の 中 に 重 要 な ⾳ が あ り 、 そ れを 囲 む ⾳ す べ て が 「 主 要 ⾳ 」 だ","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"Within a flowing line [流れる線], there is one important tone [音]. With this tone in the center, I call all sounds that surround it Hauptton [主要音].","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1])","term":"音 oto"}
{"id":39,"lang":"ja","text":"これは笛であるため、音程の跳躍がはなはだしいが、それを筝曲のばあいのように、オクターヴを同音と考えて見ると、案外旋律的な動きとなる.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 14]","en_tr":"Because this melody is for a flute, the intervallic leaps are extreme, but as in the case with koto music, if you think of octaves as equivalent, its movement becomes surprisingly conjunct.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [9.2]","term":"オクタ okutāvu"}
{"id":40,"lang":"ja","text":"しか し新し いメディアの音楽、たとえばコン ピュータ音楽、そういった創作では演奏 家とのつながりがないと思うのですが、 そういうことに関して、先生のご意見は ございませんか。簡単にいえば、コンピ ュータ音楽はどう思われますか。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 61]","en_tr":"But compositions in new media, for example, computer music, do not have much relationship with the performers. What do you think about this aspect? In short, what do you think about computer music?","en_cite":"Park (2024) [7.2]","term":"コンピ ュータ音楽 konpi ~yūta ongaku"}
{"id":41,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"管弦楽曲 kangengakkyoku"}
{"id":42,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical [scalar] rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1, brackets added separately]","term":"音階法 onkaihō"}
{"id":43,"lang":"ja","text":"う で す 。 厳 格 な 雅 楽 の ⾳ 楽 の 組 み ⽅ と 、 哲 学 的 な 内 容 と 、 そ れ か ら 流 暢 に 流 れ る 線 的 な 美 し さ を 、 た と え ば 南 道 唱 と か 歌 曲 と い っ た 形 式 の ⼀ 連 の 声 楽 が あ り ま す が 、 そ う い う と こ ろ か ら た く さ ん 学 び ま し た 。 そ こ に 、 今 度 は 線 的 な 動 き ⽅ の ⾳ 楽 的 な 理 論 を ⼤ 系 づ け ま し た.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"Yes. I learned a lot from A-ak's strict organization and philosophical content, and vocal music's smoothly flowing linear beauty, such as Namdo Chang and Gagok [가곡], or other vocal genres.Based on these, I organized my own musical theory of linear motion.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"声楽が koe raku ga"}
{"id":44,"lang":"ja","text":"まず童唄、民謡の類は、すでにわれわれの出発点であった。長唄については上に述べた通り、この核音の支配が顕著にあらわれているが、譜27は哥沢の例で、hとeとに現われた核音は、明瞭に旋律構造の骨格をなしている。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 8]","en_tr":"First, our points of departure were children's songs and folk songs. As I have said above about nagauta, nuclear tones strikingly control the melodies, but example 27 (Example 4) is an example of utazawa, and the pitches B and E clearly make up the skeleton of the melody's construction as its nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [5.2].","term":"哥沢 utazawa"}
{"id":45,"lang":"ja","text":"核音の比較音楽学的意味については第4節でのべるが、西洋音楽一般についてはこれにあたるものを見ない。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 5]","en_tr":"I will discuss the meanings of nuclear tones in comparative musicology in section 4, but in Western music, we do not generally see things like this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3]","term":"比較音楽学 hikaku ongakugaku"}
{"id":46,"lang":"ja","text":"機械を幾ら使っても、 機械から出る音楽は機械がつくるんです から、そこには血が流れないんです。こ れは大原則として、音楽には人間の血と 精神が通じてなければならない。究極は 人間の血と精神だと思います、純粋な考 え方をすれば。ぼくが亡びても、人間の血と精神はともに残るでしょう。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 61]","en_tr":"No matter how much a machine can do, the music coming from the machine is made by the machine. No blood flows through the music. This is a fundamental principle. Music must channel human blood and spirit. Ultimately, I think music is human blood and spirit. To speak naively, a person's blood and spirit will remain even after my death.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [7.2]","term":"血 chi"}
{"id":47,"lang":"ja","text":"「時」の考え方が形式観に反映した 例として西洋ではソナタ形式があります が、ソナタ形式ですと、第一主題部があ り、第二主題部がある。これらは対立し た区間であり、第二主題の部分は第一主 題と異なった時間を独自に形成するわけ ですから、瞬間に世界を持つ陰陽とは全 く異なるということですね。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"The Sonata form might be one example that reflects the Western formalistic view of time. In Sonata form, there are primary and secondary theme areas. They are contrasting sections that independently develop [the sense of] time. Therefore, it is completely different from yin and yang, which contain an eternity in a moment.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.2]","term":"第一主題部 dai ichi shudaibu"}
{"id":48,"lang":"ja","text":"ですから、先生の作品が終わりに近づくにつれ、それらが高い次死で融合して、一体のものであるということが非常に強く示されるという感動的なコーダをいつも聴くことができるんだと思うのですが、そういったものと感じてよろしいんでし.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 52)","en_tr":"For this reason, toward the end of your works, they [the seemingly conflicting elements] are fused in a higher dimension and strongly express their bodily unity [一体]. That seems to be the reason why I always hear deeply moving codas.","en_cite":"(Park (2024)  [2.2])","term":"一体 Ittai"}
{"id":49,"lang":"ja","text":"そしてdisとaisによる支配楽句の区分は比較的細かいけれども、上にのべたような意味で、終止音としての意味を持たないと考えられたばあいの出現を無視すると、第1行目は全体的にdisの支配下にあり、第2行目はaisの支配下にあると見ていい。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 2]","en_tr":"Although I have narrowly divided the melody into phrases [phrasal divisions] controlled by D♯ and A♯ in a similar way to what I said above, if we ignore cases that I don't think hold meaning as ending notes, we can see that the first line is entirely controlled by D♯, and the second line by A♯.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.3, brackets added separately]","term":"楽句の区分 gakuku no kubun"}
{"id":50,"lang":"ja","text":"「ハウプト・トン」における陰と陽の相 対的な変化は、微細な時間によるとらえ 方から巨大な時間によるとらえ方までい ろいろな段階があります。そこでは瞬間 に永遠が反映され、永遠を瞬間としてつ かむことができるわけです。それが東洋人の「時」の考え方で、西 洋人の「時」の考え方と全く違うところ なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"In the case of a Hauptton, the relative change between yin and yang can be understood through various steps from micro-timing or macro-timing. In it, a moment reflects eternity, and eternity can be captured as a moment. That is the Eastern way of thinking about time (時), which is completely different from the Western conception of time.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"時 toki"}
{"id":51,"lang":"ja","text":"最後に、先生の作品は演奏家という媒体を通じて聴衆に伝えられるわけで すから、演奏家との深い信頼関係と、演 奏家の全人格に対しての信頼に基づいて つくられているものだと思います。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 61]","en_tr":"In closing, your compositions reach the listening public through performers, which, I think, is grounded upon a deeply trusting relationship between you and the performers and faith in the performer's whole personality.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [7.2]","term":"演奏家 ensōka"}
{"id":52,"lang":"ja","text":"そ し て 韓 国 に は 厳 格 な⽴ 場 を と る 雅 楽 ⾳ 楽 と は 別 に 、 宮 廷 ⾳ 楽 で も 寺 院 ⾳ 楽 で も な い 、⼀ 般 ⼤ 衆 と 上 流 社 会 が 共 有 し て き た 、 西 洋 に ⾒ ら れ る よ う な 知 識 社 会 で 楽 し ん で き た ⾳ 楽 世 界 が ま だ あ り ま す 。 そ れ か ら ま た 芸 術 歌 曲 、芸 術 民 謡 と い い ま す か 、 そ う い う も の が あ り ま す","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"In addition, there is a vernacular musical tradition in Korea that is neither court music nor ritual music, which had been enjoyed by both the commoners and the aristocrats, similar to the musical sphere you would see in Western intellectuals. In addition to A-ak, which takes a strict stance, there are Korean art songs and folk music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"⾳楽世界 yīn-Raku yo-kai"}
{"id":53,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4]","term":"中心音 chūshin-on"}
{"id":54,"lang":"ja","text":"\"動は静であり、静は動であるというのが私の音楽の総括的な見方だ.\" (Yun (1984) - Japanese 52). \"「ハウプト・トン」は二つあるときも多いのです。二つあれば、それは陰陽関 係を持ちます。たとえば、動と静の関係 であったりします。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"Motion [動] is stillness [靜] and stillness [靜] is motion [動], it is my music's overall perspective.\" Park (2024) [2]. \"It is often the case that there are two Haupttones. When there are two, they form a relationship of yin and yang. For example, it is also a relationship between motion (動) and stillness (靜).","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"静 sei"}
{"id":55,"lang":"ja","text":"メタフィジカルじゃないけれども、たとえば《レアク》は雅楽の要素を持っています。韓国でもそう、日本でもそうですけれども、雅楽はほとんど人間世界。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"It is not metaphysical, per se. For example, Reak contains elements from A-ak. It is the case in both Korea and Japan that A-ak largely expresses the world mostly beyond the human realm for me.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5.2]","term":"メタフィジカル metafijikaru"}
{"id":56,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし鎌倉・室町時代に興った能楽の譜では、この点がはなはだ不正確で、絶対音高を表示する譜面によってはとらえることが困難である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"However, in the sheet music of nō, which became prosperous in the Kamakura [1185 – 1333 CE] and Muromachi [1336 – 1573 CE] periods, the notes are extremely imprecise, and it is difficult to capture absolute pitch from what is displayed in the sheet music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.1]","term":"不正確 fuseikaku "}
{"id":57,"lang":"ja","text":"たとえば長唄の「老松」では、かりに本調子を3本にとると(三味線の第1弦をHに合わせる)、譜26のようになる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"For example, in the nagauta \"Oimatsu (Old Pine),\" if we take honchōshi on the third string (in which it matches the first string of the shamisen, which is tuned to B), it will be transcribed as in example 26 (Example 3).\" Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]. \"Honchōshi 本調子 is the most basic shamisen tuning, which puts the strings at roughly B-E-B.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [footnote 6]","term":"本調子 hon chōshi"}
{"id":58,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし、私の取扱おうとする素材は、単にそのように出来上った芸術音楽ばかりでなく、もっとトニカの不明瞭な民俗的素材をもふくむわけだし、またその点でさらに困難な琉球・朝鮮・中国をはじめ、アジア一般の音組織にもこの概念を適用させようとする上、後に詳しく説明するような、4度構造のテトラコルドを単位として旋律を分析するばあいの、「枠になる重要な音」として、この核音がオクターヴの中に2~3個現われることもありうるので、中心音という、何か一元的な響きの言葉では、狭くなりすぎるようにも思える。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"However, the materials that I intend to handle are not simply art musics that are already established, but also include folk musics in which the tonic pitch is less clear. Also, to take that point further, starting with the Ryukyus, Korea, and China (which pose some difficulty), I want to apply this concept to a generalized organization of notes in Asian music, and explain them afterward in detail, analyzing their melodies using the unit of the tetrachord, which spans the interval of a fourth. In such cases, two or three of these nuclear tones can appear within an octave as \"important notes that make a melodic frame.\" For that reason, the word \"central tone\" has a somewhat one-dimensional ring to it, and I think its meaning is too narrow.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4]","term":"テトラコルド tetorakorudo"}
{"id":59,"lang":"ja","text":"ただ筝曲や尺八のような器楽には、非常に自由な旋律の跳躍が見られ、核音の支配から脱しているかのように思える.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 9]","en_tr":"In instrumental music such as pieces for the koto or shakuhachi, we can see extraordinary freedom of melodic leaps, and so one may think that they have broken away from the control of their nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [6.1]","term":"筝曲 sōkyoku"}
{"id":60,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"管弦 kangen"}
{"id":61,"lang":"ja","text":"も ち ろ ん こ れ は 線 的 な も の な ん で す 。 単 ⾳ 的 な 意 味 で す 。 単 旋 律 的 な 意 味 で す 。 し か し 、 今 度 は 単 旋 律 と い う 要 素 が 重 な る と 、 主 要 ⾳ 響 に な る わ け で す 。 線 が 束 に な っ て 流 れ て い る こ と に な り ま す 。 だ か ら 、⼀ つ ⼀ つ か ら す れ ば 主 要 ⾳ で あ り 、 束 に な っ て 流 れ れ ば 主 要 ⾳ 響 で あ り ま す 。 そ し て そ れ ら の ⼀ つ ⼀ つが 似 て い る わ け で す 。 似 て い て 、 し か も 全 体 が 同 ⼀ 性 を 持 っ て い る と い う こ と で す.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 52)","en_tr":"It refers to a singular note and a singular melodic line. But when linear elements are stacked, they become Hauptklang [主要音響].(7) Lines become a bundle and begin to flow. In short, each line is Hauptton, and when it is bundled and flows it is Hauptklang. In other words, each of the lines is analogous while the whole is uniform.","en_cite":"(Park (2024)  [1.7])","term":"主要音響 shuyō onkyō"}
{"id":62,"lang":"ja","text":"また1つの核音の支配圏から脱して他の核音の圏に移るには、それだけの旋律構成上の力がなければならない。したがって核音による区分の縦線は、その次に来る旋律の跳躍的な力を意味する重要な句節法となる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 6]","en_tr":"Also, in order to escape one nuclear tone's sphere of control and move to another nuclear tone's sphere, the melody must be strongly constructed. Therefore, the vertical lines that I have drawn to divide these melodies by their governing nuclear tones can be seen as illustrating an important phrasal principle, which indicates how the upcoming melody will be able to leap [leaping power].","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3, brackets added separately]","term":"跳躍的な力 chōyaku tekina chikara"}
{"id":63,"lang":"ja","text":"先生が獄中で書かれたオペラのことですが、先生は健康も害されて、その オペラ自体は演奏される見通しすらない し、その作品自体が獄中から出れるかど うかもわからない、そういった中で、意 識を超越して一気にお書きになったとう かがったのですが。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 59]","en_tr":"Regarding the opera you had composed while in prison [Die Witwe des Schmetterlings (Butterfly Widow)], at the time, you were in poor health, there was no perspective for its performance, and you weren't even sure whether you could transport the score outside of the prison cell. How were you able to overcome senses [意識] and compose in these circumstances with one stroke?","en_cite":"Park (2024) [6.1]","term":"意識 ishiki"}
{"id":64,"lang":"ja","text":"西村それで私が少し感じるのは、これは全く当たっていないかもしれませんが、ヘテロフォニーという考え方がございま すね。あれは非常に単純に割り切った言い方をしてしまえば、主になる旋律と、同時に装飾的なものが存在する。一つの本質のものが、同時に多像をとりながら共存していくのが、ヘテロフォニーの形だと思うんですが、先生がいまおっしゃったことからすると、その「ハウプト・トン」とヘテロフォニーとは関係があるのではないでしょうか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 52)","en_tr":"I have sensed from your description, maybe I am off-topic here, but do you know the term \"heterophony\"? To put it concisely, it means the coexistence of the main melody and an embellishing melody. I think, in heterophony, an essential idea simultaneously takes various appearances [상, 像] and they coexist. Based on what you have described, wouldn't there be a correlation between the Hauptton concept and heterophony?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.1])","term":"ヘテロフォニーheterofonī"}
{"id":65,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の 線 的 な 語 法 の も と に な っ て い る わ け で す ね 。 微 分 ⾳ 的 な 細 か い 揺 れ か ら 3 度 以 上 の シ ェ イ ク に ⾄ る よ う な 、 独 特 な 線 の 動 き は 、 韓 国 の 歌 唱 の ⽅ 法 か ら ⽣ み 出 さ れ た も の と 考 え て い い わ け で す ね .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"That underlies your linear [線的] musical language [語法]. It would be reasonable to say that the characteristic linear movements, ranging from fine microtonal tremors to tremolos wider than a third, come from the Korean singing [歌唱] style.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":" 歌唱 kashō"}
{"id":66,"lang":"ja","text":"ピアノもないし、机もないし、 鉛筆と紙だけだったんです。それからテ キスト。私がそういう状態でも音符を書 かなければならなかったのは、自分が死 んでしまえば、自分の中に残っているた くさんの音楽は自分とともに死んでしま う。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 60]","en_tr":"No piano, no desk, only pencil and paper. And the text. The reason why I could not stop writing the notes even in that situation was that if I die then and there, the music in me also dies.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [6.3]","term":"ピアノ piano"}
{"id":67,"lang":"ja","text":"流 れ る 線 の 中 に 重 要 な ⾳ が あ り 、 そ れを 囲 む ⾳ す べ て が 「 主 要 ⾳ 」 だ","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"Within a flowing line [流れる線], there is one important tone [音]. With this tone in the center, I call all sounds that surround it Hauptton [主要音].","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1])","term":"流れる線 Nagareru sen"}
{"id":68,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical [scalar] rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1, brackets added separately]","term":"音階 onkai"}
{"id":69,"lang":"ja","text":"だから、そういうイマジ ネーションが、ところどころにつかめる だけなんです。しかし、私にとっては作 曲家としてそういうようなファンタジー を持つことが、創作の大きな力となって います。純粋な音だけによって、一九六 ○年代から七〇年の初期まで作曲をしま した。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 59]","en_tr":"In other words, those imaginations are only captured here and there. As a composer, however, those fantastical stories greatly aid my creative process. I had been composing with pure sounds [absolute music?] from the 1960s until the early 1970s.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5.2]","term":"純粋な音 junsuina oto"}
{"id":70,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 今 度 は 器 楽 曲 に 移 り ま し て 、 す べ て の 器 楽 曲 は ま ず 声 楽 から 受 け 継 い で 、 そ れ を 発 展 さ せ た も の とい っ て も い い わ け で す 。 た と え ば 「 ⽝ 等 」と い い ま し て 、 横 笛 を ⾧ く し た 形 の 韓 国 の 民 族 楽 器 が あ り ま し て 、 そ れ で 奏 さ れ る 節 回 し は 歌 唱 を 受 け 継 い だ も の で す 。そ し て 、 そ こ に は 線 的 な ⾳ 楽 の 妙 味 が ある わ け で す.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"And it also expands to instrumental music. One could say that all instrumental music is developed by continuing ideas from vocal music. For example, a flute-like instrument made with bamboo [橫笛] called Dae-gum is one of the Korean traditional instruments. Melodies played by that instrument are inherited from singing. They have their own charm of linear music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.5])","term":"節回 bushi kai"}
{"id":71,"lang":"ja","text":"そ し て 韓 国 に は 厳 格 な⽴ 場 を と る 雅 楽 ⾳ 楽 と は 別 に 、 宮 廷 ⾳ 楽 で も 寺 院 ⾳ 楽 で も な い 、⼀ 般 ⼤ 衆 と 上 流 社 会 が 共 有 し て き た 、 西 洋 に ⾒ ら れ る よ う な 知 識 社 会 で 楽 し ん で き た ⾳ 楽 世 界 が ま だ あ り ま す 。 そ れ か ら ま た 芸 術 歌 曲 、芸 術 民 謡 と い い ま す か 、 そ う い う も の が あ り ま す","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"In addition, there is a vernacular musical tradition in Korea that is neither court music nor ritual music, which had been enjoyed by both the commoners and the aristocrats, similar to the musical sphere you would see in Western intellectuals. In addition to A-ak, which takes a strict stance, there are Korean art songs and folk music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"寺院⾳楽 Tera in yīn Raku"}
{"id":72,"lang":"ja","text":"走り ながら、今度は生命力を、緊張力を高め るためにヴィヴラートを生じさせるわけで す。ヴィヴラートによって、集中力と緊張 感を増します。そしてメリスマ的な要素 が加わります。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"As it runs, it creates vibratos in order to heighten its lifeforce and tension. Through vibrato, the concentration and tension are increased. And melismatic elements are added.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"緊張力 kinchōryoku"}
{"id":73,"lang":"ja","text":"ただ筝曲や尺八のような器楽には、非常に自由な旋律の跳躍が見られ、核音の支配から脱しているかのように思える.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 9]","en_tr":"In instrumental music such as pieces for the koto or shakuhachi, we can see extraordinary freedom of melodic leaps, and so one may think that they have broken away from the control of their nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [6.1]","term":"尺八 shakuhachi"}
{"id":74,"lang":"ja","text":"この核音は、民謡よりもむしろ芸術音楽ことに能楽の謡や三味線声楽の長唄などでは非常にはっきりとした形で現われており、そのばあいの旋律は、ただある1つの核音をめぐって上下浮動するという状態である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"These nuclear tones appear extremely clearly in Japanese art music, especially in the utai of nō music and shamisen vocal music like nagauta, even more than in folk songs. The melodies in those (art music) cases have the characteristic of revolving around only one nuclear tone, and bobbing up and down around it.\" Hynes-Tawa (2024)  [2.1]. \"Utai 謡, while etymologically meaning simply \"song,\" has come to refer specifically to the vocal music of the nō 能 theater tradition. It is accompanied by a hayashi 囃子 ensemble, which consists of a few drums and a flute.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [footnote 4]","term":"能楽 nōgaku"}
{"id":75,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"声楽曲 Seigaku"}
{"id":76,"lang":"ja","text":"「ハウプト・トン」は二つあるときも多いのです。二つあれば、それは陰陽関 係を持ちます。たとえば、動と静の関係 であったりします。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"It is often the case that there are two Haupttones. When there are two, they form a relationship of yin and yang. For example, it is also a relationship between motion (動) and stillness (靜).","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"陽 hi"}
{"id":77,"lang":"ja","text":"さて、核音の旋律中におけるこのような支配は、伝統音楽のそれぞれのジャンルにどのように現われているだろうか、雅楽輸入以前の音楽をわれわれは正確に知ることができないし、現在残っているものでも、起原の古いものは、時代が経過するにつれて、多少改変させられたかも知れない。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 8]","en_tr":"Now then, how does the control over melodies that nuclear tones have manifest in various different genres of traditional music? We cannot know anything for certain about music before the importation of gagaku, and even that old original music that does remain in the present has probably undergone some change as eras have passed.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [5.1]","term":"雅楽 gagaku"}
{"id":78,"lang":"ja","text":"まず、装飾音です。装飾音から始めて、 だんだん揺れが大きくなって、場合によ ってはヴィヴラートが4度までいきます。 スタートする音に力を集めるために、装 飾音があるわけで、それ自体に意味はな いわけです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"Now, it is a decorative tone. Beginning from the decorative tone, the trembling grows larger and, at times, the vibrato gets as wide as a fourth. The decorative tone exists to concentrate on the tone's beginning, and it is meaningless by itself.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"ヴィブラート vu~iburāto"}
{"id":79,"lang":"ja","text":"純粋な音自体を持って、人間の現世を超越した、そういう人間世界と天空の世界の中間、人間世界と天空の世界の接触といいますか、あるいは地 獄のというように、全く人間の現世の世 界とは離れて、超越した宇宙の問題を取 り扱った、そういう作品は他にもたくさ んあります。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 59]","en_tr":"The realm that is in between the mortal world and the celestial world, or perhaps a contact between the two worlds. There are many other compositions that deal with a topic that is separate from the real world, such as purgatory and a transcendent universe.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5.3]","term":"人間世界 ningen sekai"}
{"id":80,"lang":"ja","text":"リズム・旋律法・多声性・楽器編成などあらゆる点でその他のジャンルと異なる","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 14]","en_tr":"All aspects such as rhythm, melodic system, polyphony, and instrumental organization differ from other genres.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [8.2]","term":"多声性 ōzei-sei"}
{"id":81,"lang":"ja","text":"「ハウプト・トン」における陰と陽の相 対的な変化は、微細な時間によるとらえ 方から巨大な時間によるとらえ方までい ろいろな段階があります。そこでは瞬間 に永遠が反映され、永遠を瞬間としてつ かむことができるわけです。それが東洋人の「時」の考え方で、西 洋人の「時」の考え方と全く違うところ なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"In the case of a Hauptton, the relative change between yin and yang can be understood through various steps from micro-timing or macro-timing. In it, a moment reflects eternity, and eternity can be captured as a moment. That is the Eastern way of thinking about time (時), which is completely different from the Western conception of time.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"微細な時間 bisaina jikan"}
{"id":82,"lang":"ja","text":"機械を幾ら使っても、 機械から出る音楽は機械がつくるんです から、そこには血が流れないんです。こ れは大原則として、音楽には人間の血と 精神が通じてなければならない。究極は 人間の血と精神だと思います、純粋な考 え方をすれば。ぼくが亡びても、人間の血と精神はともに残るでしょう。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 61]","en_tr":"No matter how much a machine can do, the music coming from the machine is made by the machine. No blood flows through the music. This is a fundamental principle. Music must channel human blood and spirit. Ultimately, I think music is human blood and spirit. To speak naively, a person's blood and spirit will remain even after my death.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [7.2]","term":"精神 seishin"}
{"id":83,"lang":"ja","text":"まず低い音から始まります。Bbの音で、 これは暗い音なんです。無から生まれる。 実はこれはピアニッシモなんですけれど も。これは暗示です。まだ音じゃないわ けなんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"First of all, it begins with a low pitch [Example 1]. With the Bb, it is a dark tone. It emerges from nothing. Although it is in pianissimo, it is an implication [暗示]. It is not yet a tone.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"暗い kurai"}
{"id":84,"lang":"ja","text":"瞬間に永遠が反映され、永遠を瞬間と してつかむ―東洋人の考え方です。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 56]","en_tr":"A moment reflects eternity, and the eternity can be captured as a moment.","en_cite":"Park (2024)  [4]","term":"瞬間 shunkan"}
{"id":85,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし、私の取扱おうとする素材は、単にそのように出来上った芸術音楽ばかりでなく、もっとトニカの不明瞭な民俗的素材をもふくむわけだし、またその点でさらに困難な琉球・朝鮮・中国をはじめ、アジア一般の音組織にもこの概念を適用させようとする上、後に詳しく説明するような、4度構造のテトラコルドを単位として旋律を分析するばあいの、「枠になる重要な音」として、この核音がオクターヴの中に2~3個現われることもありうるので、中心音という、何か一元的な響きの言葉では、狭くなりすぎるようにも思える。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"However, the materials that I intend to handle are not simply art musics that are already established, but also include folk musics in which the tonic pitch is less clear. Also, to take that point further, starting with the Ryukyus, Korea, and China (which pose some difficulty), I want to apply this concept to a generalized organization of notes in Asian music, and explain them afterward in detail, analyzing their melodies using the unit of the tetrachord, which spans the interval of a fourth. In such cases, two or three of these nuclear tones can appear within an octave as \"important notes that make a melodic frame.\" For that reason, the word \"central tone\" has a somewhat one-dimensional ring to it, and I think its meaning is too narrow.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4]","term":"民俗的素材 minzoku teki sozai"}
{"id":86,"lang":"ja","text":"う で す 。 厳 格 な 雅 楽 の ⾳ 楽 の 組 み ⽅ と 、 哲 学 的 な 内 容 と 、 そ れ か ら 流 暢 に 流 れ る 線 的 な 美 し さ を 、 た と え ば 南 道 唱 と か 歌 曲 と い っ た 形 式 の ⼀ 連 の 声 楽 が あ り ま す が 、 そ う い う と こ ろ か ら た く さ ん 学 び ま し た 。 そ こ に 、 今 度 は 線 的 な 動 き ⽅ の ⾳ 楽 的 な 理 論 を ⼤ 系 づ け ま し た.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"Yes. I learned a lot from A-ak's strict organization and philosophical content, and vocal music's smoothly flowing linear beauty, such as Namdo Chang and Gagok [가곡], or other vocal genres.(4) Based on these, I organized my own musical theory of linear motion.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"歌曲 uta kyoku"}
{"id":87,"lang":"ja","text":"このようなばあい、終止音は一方からは単に楽曲の終止音としての意味ばかりでなく、旋律線の上下動における中核的な意味を持つという理由で、他方では、連続的にくり返されるべき性質の「数え唄」や「網引唄」の中には、かならずしも終止音に終らない旋律も多いという理由で(そのばあいですら旋律線の中核的意味を失わない)、終止音とよぶより中核音または単に核音とよぶ方が適当ではないだろうか。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"In cases like these, the ending note on the one hand holds meaning not only as a simple ending note to the piece, but also holds meaning as a central nucleus of upward and downward movement in the melodic line. On the other hand, among songs like \"Counting Song\" and \"Net-Pulling Song\" whose melodies tend to be repeated continuously, there are many songs with melodies that certainly do not end on the ending note (even in those cases, the ending notes do not lose the meaning of a central nucleus of the melodic line). For that reason, rather than calling them ending notes, it may be more appropriate to call them central nuclear tones or simply nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]","term":"中核音/核音 chukaku-on/kaku-on"}
{"id":88,"lang":"ja","text":"\"動は静であり、静は動であるというのが私の音楽の総括的な見方だ.\" (Yun (1984) - Japanese, 52). \"「ハウプト・トン」は二つあるときも多いのです。二つあれば、それは陰陽関 係を持ちます。たとえば、動と静の関係 であったりします。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"Motion [動] is stillness [靜] and stillness [靜] is motion [動], it is my music's overall perspective.\" Park (2024) [2]. \"It is often the case that there are two Haupttones. When there are two, they form a relationship of yin and yang. For example, it is also a relationship between motion (動) and stillness (靜).","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"動 dō"}
{"id":89,"lang":"ja","text":"走り ながら、今度は生命力を、緊張力を高め るためにヴィヴラートを生じさせるわけで す。ヴィヴラートによって、集中力と緊張 感を増します。そしてメリスマ的な要素 が加わります。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"As it runs, it creates vibratos in order to heighten its lifeforce and tension. Through vibrato, the concentration and tension are increased. And melismatic elements are added.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"生命力 seimeiryoku"}
{"id":90,"lang":"ja","text":"核音の比較音楽学的意味については第4節でのべるが、西洋音楽一般についてはこれにあたるものを見ない。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 5]","en_tr":"I will discuss the meanings of nuclear tones in comparative musicology in section 4, but in Western music, we do not generally see things like this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3]","term":"西洋音楽 seiyō ongaku"}
{"id":91,"lang":"ja","text":"\"しかし、私の音楽が長時間緊張感を保っているということは、全くそのとおりなんです。私の音楽の根本をなしている線的な要素が、巧妙に持続性を持っており、そのナチュール自体が、持続の無限な可能性を持っているのです。たとえば能の音楽とか歌舞伎のように、何時間同じ線を聴いても絶対飽きない秘密がこれなんです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"But it is true that my pieces maintain tension for a long time. The foundation of my music, the linear element possesses a deft persistence. That \"nature\" [ナチュール] itself enables the unlimited persistence. For example, the secret of not being bored while listening to the same line for hours, like Noh [能] or Kabuki [歌舞技] is this.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"緊張 kinchō"}
{"id":92,"lang":"ja","text":"譜25のAは、任意に拾いあげた民謡の一例を、楽譜の上段には終止音gとdにより、それぞれ支配的な楽句を区分し、下段には終止音間の4度音程と5度音程によって、それぞれの占める楽句を区分したものである。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"Example 25A (Example 1) takes an arbitrarily-chosen example of a folk song, and above the notation divides the various musical phrases into those controlled by the ending note G and those controlled by D. Below it, it divides the phrases bounded by the interval of a fourth from those bounded by a fifth.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"民謡 min’yō"}
{"id":93,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 今 度 は 器 楽 曲 に 移 り ま し て 、 す べ て の 器 楽 曲 は ま ず 声 楽 から 受 け 継 い で 、 そ れ を 発 展 さ せ た も の とい っ て も い い わ け で す 。 た と え ば 「 ⽝ 等 」と い い ま し て 、 横 笛 を ⾧ く し た 形 の 韓 国 の 民 族 楽 器 が あ り ま し て 、 そ れ で 奏 さ れ る 節 回 し は 歌 唱 を 受 け 継 い だ も の で す 。そ し て 、 そ こ に は 線 的 な ⾳ 楽 の 妙 味 が ある わ け で す.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"And it also expands to instrumental music. One could say that all instrumental music is developed by continuing ideas from vocal music. For example, a flute-like instrument made with bamboo [橫笛] called Dae-gum is one of the Korean traditional instruments. Melodies played by that instrument are inherited from singing. They have their own charm of linear music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.5])","term":"妙味 myō aji"}
{"id":94,"lang":"ja","text":"\"しかし、私の音楽が長時間緊張感を保っているということは、全くそのとおりなんです。私の音楽の根本をなしている線的な要素が、巧妙に持続性を持っており、そのナチュール自体が、持続の無限な可能性を持っているのです。たとえば能の音楽とか歌舞伎のように、何時間同じ線を聴いても絶対飽きない秘密がこれなんです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"But it is true that my pieces maintain tension for a long time. The foundation of my music, the linear element possesses a deft persistence. That \"nature\" [ナチュール] itself enables the unlimited persistence. For example, the secret of not being bored while listening to the same line for hours, like Noh [能] or Kabuki [歌舞技] is this.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"能 no"}
{"id":95,"lang":"ja","text":"しかもこれによってわれわれは、「音楽における日本的なもの」の1つの側面を確実にとらえることができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 15]","en_tr":"Furthermore, with this melodic construction based on nuclear tones we can reliably consider this as one aspect of \"Japaneseness in music.\"","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [10]","term":"日本的なもの Nihon-tekina mono"}
{"id":96,"lang":"ja","text":"この関係をもっと明らかにするために掲げたのがBの例で、この盆踊唄は終始dis―aisという4度音程の支配下にある。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 2]","en_tr":"I have brought out example B in order to make this relationship clearer. This bon-odori song from beginning to end is under the control of the interval of a fourth between D♯ and A♯.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.2]","term":"盆踊唄 bon’odori uta"}
{"id":97,"lang":"ja","text":"譜25のAは、任意に拾いあげた民謡の一例を、楽譜の上段には終止音gとdにより、それぞれ支配的な楽句を区分し、下段には終止音間の4度音程と5度音程によって、それぞれの占める楽句を区分したものである。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"Example 25A (Example 1) takes an arbitrarily-chosen example of a folk song, and above the notation divides the various musical phrases into those controlled by the ending note G and those controlled by D. Below it, it divides the phrases bounded by the interval of a fourth from those bounded by a fifth.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"楽譜 gakufu"}
{"id":98,"lang":"ja","text":"つぎに掲げた譜29はこの点を充分考慮した上で田中正平博士によって採譜されたものである.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"Example 29, which I'll bring up next, was transcribed by the scholar Tanaka Shōhei after he had thought thoroughly about these points.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.1]","term":"採譜 saifu"}
{"id":99,"lang":"ja","text":"日本の作曲家たちは、従来、作曲のマテリアルは、現代でも古い西洋の伝統的な形式観に何かしら沿っているのではないでしょうか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"Perhaps Japanese composers follow the old Western traditional formalism even though the compositional materials [マテリアル] might be modern.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"作曲のマテリアル sakkyoku no materiaru"}
{"id":100,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"邦楽 hōgaku"}
{"id":101,"lang":"ja","text":"そこで音楽史の順序とは逆に、もっとも身ぢかに存在するものから調べてゆくことにする。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 8]","en_tr":"Thus in opposition to the usual order of music history, I have decided to begin my investigation from what exists close at hand.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [5.1]","term":"音楽史 ongakushi"}
{"id":102,"lang":"ja","text":"これはクセとよばれる部分の一部であるが、その4度音程をもつ上下動の中にも明瞭に核音の支配をうかがい知ることができる。これと同じ旋律的な弱吟という発声法によるクセの他の部分では、これよりもはるかに一語一音符的な(syllabic)スタイルによっており、","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"This is one part of something that might be called the kuse, and within the up-and-down motion across the interval of a fourth, we can clearly perceive the control of nuclear tones. In another part of the kuse, whose method of vocalization is called melodic yowagin, it is in a far more syllabic style (one word to one note) even than this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2]","term":"クセ kuse"}
{"id":103,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical [scalar] rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1, brackets added separately]","term":"要素 yōso"}
{"id":104,"lang":"ja","text":"この音 には装飾音が欠けています。しかし、三 連符の頭の休符がそれにかわる働きをし ます。それに続いてメリスマ的な要素が ありますね。これはもう少し発展した「ハ ウプト・トン」のあり方なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"There is no decorative tone for this. But the first rest of the triplet substitutes its role. It is followed by a melismatic element. This is a more developed figure of a Hauptton.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"要素 yōso"}
{"id":105,"lang":"ja","text":"これはクセとよばれる部分の一部であるが、その4度音程をもつ上下動の中にも明瞭に核音の支配をうかがい知ることができる。これと同じ旋律的な弱吟という発声法によるクセの他の部分では、これよりもはるかに一語一音符的な(syllabic)スタイルによっており、","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"This is one part of something that might be called the kuse, and within the up-and-down motion across the interval of a fourth, we can clearly perceive the control of nuclear tones. In another part of the kuse, whose method of vocalization is called melodic yowagin, it is in a far more syllabic style (one word to one note) even than this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2]","term":"一語一 ichigo ichi"}
{"id":106,"lang":"ja","text":"たとえば長唄の「老松」では、かりに本調子を3本にとると(三味線の第1弦をHに合わせる)、譜26のようになる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"For example, in the nagauta \"Oimatsu (Old Pine),\" if we take honchōshi on the third string (in which it matches the first string of the shamisen, which is tuned to B), it will be transcribed as in example 26 (Example 3).","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]","term":"弦 gen"}
{"id":107,"lang":"ja","text":"だから、私の音楽はすべてが流れる、流暢に流れる、その線のたゆまない繰り返しだと言えます。その流暢に流れている線が直線ではなくて、湾曲しているんです。しかも湾曲の仕方が多様なんです。その湾曲の中にもいろいろな部分があって、この湾曲の中にさらに部分、部分、部分があって、それ自体がこの湾曲から比べれば、一つの世界になる。その一つの世界の中に、また世界がある。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 54)","en_tr":"Therefore, people speak about my music as flowing, smoothly flowing, an endless repetition of the line. The smoothly flowing line is not a straight line but is a curved line (彎曲). And there are various ways a line can be curved. \"Within a curve, there are various parts. The part and the curve each contain a universe within itself. It means that within a universe, there is another universe.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.4])","term":"彎曲 wankokyu"}
{"id":108,"lang":"ja","text":"核音の比較音楽学的意味については第4節でのべるが、西洋音楽一般についてはこれにあたるものを見ない。したがってヨーロッパの音楽理論の用語には、これを表現する適切な言葉がないのである。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 5]","en_tr":"I will discuss the meanings of nuclear tones in comparative musicology in section 4, but in Western music, we do not generally see things like this. Therefore, in European music theory terminology, there is no word that appropriately expresses this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3]","term":"ヨーロッパの音楽理論 Yōroppa no ongaku riron"}
{"id":109,"lang":"ja","text":"リズム・旋律法・多声性・楽器編成などあらゆる点でその他のジャンルと異なる","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 14]","en_tr":"All aspects such as rhythm, melodic system, polyphony, and instrumental organization differ from other genres.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [8.2]","term":"リズム rizumu"}
{"id":110,"lang":"ja","text":"流 れ る 線 の 中 に 重 要 な ⾳ が あ り 、 そ れを 囲 む ⾳ す べ て が 「 主 要 ⾳ 」 だ","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"Within a flowing line [流れる線], there is one important tone [音]. With this tone in the center, I call all sounds that surround it Hauptton [主要音].","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1])","term":"主要音 Shuyo-on"}
{"id":111,"lang":"ja","text":"フルート・ソロはDの音を直接スタート しないで、下からまず上がってくる。と いうと、Bの音が準備になる。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"The flute solo does not begin right on D but rises from below. Bb thus prepares it [the note D].","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"フルート furūto"}
{"id":112,"lang":"ja","text":"「時」の考え方が形式観に反映した 例として西洋ではソナタ形式があります が、ソナタ形式ですと、第一主題部があ り、第二主題部がある。これらは対立し た区間であり、第二主題の部分は第一主 題と異なった時間を独自に形成するわけ ですから、瞬間に世界を持つ陰陽とは全 く異なるということですね。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"The Sonata form might be one example that reflects the Western formalistic view of time. In Sonata form, there are primary and secondary theme areas. They are contrasting sections that independently develop [the sense of] time. Therefore, it is completely different from yin and yang, which contain an eternity in a moment.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.2]","term":"ソナタ形式 sonata keishiki"}
{"id":113,"lang":"ja","text":"このようなピッチの微分音的変化は、もとより時代がうつるにつれて加味されてきた表現法の技巧であると想像される。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 12]","en_tr":"This sort of microtonal change in pitch is imagined to have been a technique of expressive principles that, from the beginning, had changed along with movement through the ages.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2]","term":"微分音 bibun-on"}
{"id":114,"lang":"ja","text":"\"そ れ が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の 線 的 な 語 法 の も と に な っ て い る わ け で す ね 。 微 分 ⾳ 的 な 細 か い 揺 れ か ら 3 度 以 上 の シ ェ イ ク に ⾄ る よ う な 、 独 特 な 線 の 動 き は 、 韓 国 の 歌 唱 の ⽅ 法 か ら ⽣ み 出 さ れ た も の と 考 え て い い わ け で す ね 。(","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"That underlies your linear [線的] musical language [語法]. It would be reasonable to say that the characteristic linear movements, ranging from fine microtonal tremors to tremolos wider than a third, come from the Korean singing [歌唱] style.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"微分音 bibun-on"}
{"id":115,"lang":"ja","text":"本当を言えばそれを全く切り離してぼくの音楽を聴いてもらいたいけれども、ぼくは、過去の自分の経緯があるから最も人間的な芸術家でいたいんです。ぼく はかつては、作曲とはほとんど天界に近 い位置で音だけを聴いて、それに秩序を 与えることだと思っていました。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"In fact, I would like the listeners to hear my music without any of these background stories. Because my past life experience has tangled twists and turns, I hope to be the most humanistic artist. In the past, I once thought that composing music is akin to listening to tones in a near-celestial position and imbuing them with an order.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5.1]","term":"秩序 chitsujo"}
{"id":116,"lang":"ja","text":"声楽の旋律が一般に順次進行に傾き、器楽の旋律がこれに対して跳躍進行を多く含むということは","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 10]","en_tr":"That vocal melodies generally incline towards stepwise motion, and that instrumental melodies conversely include more leaping motion,","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.1]","term":"跳躍進行 chōyakushinkō"}
{"id":117,"lang":"ja","text":"この核音は、民謡よりもむしろ芸術音楽ことに能楽の謡や三味線声楽の長唄などでは非常にはっきりとした形で現われており、そのばあいの旋律は、ただある1つの核音をめぐって上下浮動するという状態である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"These nuclear tones appear extremely clearly in Japanese art music, especially in the utai of nō music and shamisen vocal music like nagauta, even more than in folk songs. The melodies in those (art music) cases have the characteristic of revolving around only one nuclear tone, and bobbing up and down around it.\" Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]. \"Utai 謡, while etymologically meaning simply \"song,\" has come to refer specifically to the vocal music of the nō 能 theater tradition. It is accompanied by a hayashi 囃子 ensemble, which consists of a few drums and a flute.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [footnote 5]","term":"長唄 nagauta"}
{"id":118,"lang":"ja","text":"これはクセとよばれる部分の一部であるが、その4度音程をもつ上下動の中にも明瞭に核音の支配をうかがい知ることができる。これと同じ旋律的な弱吟という発声法によるクセの他の部分では、これよりもはるかに一語一音符的な(syllabic)スタイルによっており、","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"This is one part of something that might be called the kuse, and within the up-and-down motion across the interval of a fourth, we can clearly perceive the control of nuclear tones. In another part of the kuse, whose method of vocalization is called melodic yowagin, it is in a far more syllabic style (one word to one note) even than this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2]","term":"弱吟 yowagin"}
{"id":119,"lang":"ja","text":"流 れ て い る 線 の 中 に 重 要 な ⾳ が あ り そ の ⾳ を 中 ⼼ と し て 、 そ れ を 囲 ん で い る ⾳ す べ て を 称 し て 私 は 「 主 要 ⾳ 」 と ⾔ い 、 学 者 た ち は「 ⼀ 様 ⾳ 」 と 呼 ん で い ま す 。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 52)","en_tr":"Within a flowing line [流れる線], there is one important tone. With this tone in the center, I call all sounds that surround it Hauptton, and the scholars call them sonic oneness.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.6])","term":"⼀様⾳ yī sama yīn"}
{"id":120,"lang":"ja","text":"譜25のAは、任意に拾いあげた民謡の一例を、楽譜の上段には終止音gとdにより、それぞれ支配的な楽句を区分し、下段には終止音間の4度音程と5度音程によって、それぞれの占める楽句を区分したものである。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"Example 25A (Example 1) takes an arbitrarily-chosen example of a folk song, and above the notation divides the various musical phrases into those controlled by the ending note G and those controlled by D. Below it, it divides the phrases bounded by the interval of a fourth from those bounded by a fifth.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"楽句 gakuku"}
{"id":121,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"ヨーロッパ Yōroppa"}
{"id":122,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"邦楽器 Hōgaku-ki"}
{"id":123,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4]","term":"調 chō"}
{"id":124,"lang":"ja","text":"Bbは、ただの準備の音です。しかし、 このDを生ませるために長3度が生じま す。長3度は明るい音程です。それで、 暗い音から明るい音になります。という ことは、少しずつ光が入ってくるという。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"The Bb is just a tone for preparation. But, in order to create D, a major third is created. A major third is a bright interval. So, a dark tone becomes a bright tone. It is like light is peeking through little by little.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"長3度 chō 3 do"}
{"id":125,"lang":"ja","text":"この音 には装飾音が欠けています。しかし、三 連符の頭の休符がそれにかわる働きをし ます。それに続いてメリスマ的な要素が ありますね。これはもう少し発展した「ハ ウプト・トン」のあり方なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"There is no decorative tone for this. But the first rest of the triplet substitutes its role. It is followed by a melismatic element. This is a more developed figure of a Hauptton.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"装飾音 sōshokuan"}
{"id":126,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European [tonal] music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4, brackets added separately]","term":"ヨーロッパの調性音楽 Yōroppa no chōsei ongaku"}
{"id":127,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"韓国の伝統楽器 Kankoku no dentō gakki"}
{"id":128,"lang":"ja","text":"江戸時代以後の音楽は一般に楽器(ことに三味線・箏・尺八)の影響によって、声楽であっても、比較的正確なピッチをもっているので、この核音のあり方を譜面の上でとらえることができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"Music from after the Edo period [1603 – 1867 CE] generally has influence from instrumental music (especially that of the shamisen, koto, or shakuhachi), and so even the vocal music has comparatively precise pitches, so one can determine the nuclear tones on its sheet music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.1]","term":"正確なピッチ seikakuna pitchi"}
{"id":129,"lang":"ja","text":"「ハウプト・トン」は二つあるときも多いのです。二つあれば、それは陰陽関 係を持ちます。たとえば、動と静の関係 であったりします。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"It is often the case that there are two Haupttones. When there are two, they form a relationship of yin and yang. For example, it is also a relationship between motion (動) and stillness (靜).","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"陰 kage"}
{"id":130,"lang":"ja","text":"その際の核音は、e(10小節)-h(2)―e(3)―h(5)―e(2)―h(4)―e(3)―h(2)―転調fis(5)―e(2)以下同様。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 4]","en_tr":"In this case, the nuclear tones would be E (for 10 measures) – B (2) – E (3) – B (5) – E (2) – B (4) – E (3) – B (2) – modulation, F♯ (5) – E (2), and it continues afterward in the same way.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.2]","term":"転調 tenchō"}
{"id":131,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の 線 的 な 語 法 の も と に な っ て い る わ け で す ね 。 微 分 ⾳ 的 な 細 か い 揺 れ か ら 3 度 以 上 の シ ェ イ ク に ⾄ る よ う な 、 独 特 な 線 の 動 き は 、 韓 国 の 歌 唱 の ⽅ 法 か ら ⽣ み 出 さ れ た も の と 考 え て い い わ け で す ね .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"That underlies your linear [線的] musical language [語法]. It would be reasonable to say that the characteristic linear movements, ranging from fine microtonal tremors to tremolos wider than a third, come from the Korean singing [歌唱] style.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"線的 sen-teki"}
{"id":132,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし、事実はもっと複雑であって、一方では次節にのべるような比較音楽学的な考察から、また他方では、雅楽輸入以前に起源を持ち、しかも現在多少とも面影をとどめていると考えられる、神楽歌や歌披講などの旋律にも明らかに核音の機能が認められるという事実から、声明にだけこの傾向の原因をもとめるわけにはゆかない.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 13]","en_tr":"On the one hand, from the perspective of comparative-musicological investigations that I will discuss in the next section; and also on the other hand from the fact that the function of nuclear tones is clearly recognized even in the melodies of kagura song and uta-hikō, which hold origins from before the importation of gagaku and furthermore are thought to retain a trace of these functioning nuclear tones in the present; we cannot go so far as to say that this is a tendency that seeks its origins only in vocal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [8.2]","term":"歌披講 uta-hikō"}
{"id":133,"lang":"ja","text":"このようなばあい、終止音は一方からは単に楽曲の終止音としての意味ばかりでなく、旋律線の上下動における中核的な意味を持つという理由で、他方では、連続的にくり返されるべき性質の「数え唄」や「網引唄」の中には、かならずしも終止音に終らない旋律も多いという理由で(そのばあいですら旋律線の中核的意味を失わない)、終止音とよぶより中核音または単に核音とよぶ方が適当ではないだろうか。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"In cases like these, the ending note on the one hand holds meaning not only as a simple ending note to the piece, but also holds meaning as a central nucleus of upward and downward movement in the melodic line. On the other hand, among songs like \"Counting Song\" and \"Net-Pulling Song\" whose melodies tend to be repeated continuously, there are many songs with melodies that certainly do not end on the ending note (even in those cases, the ending notes do not lose the meaning of a central nucleus of the melodic line). For that reason, rather than calling them ending notes, it may be more appropriate to call them central nuclear tones or simply nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]","term":"旋律線 senritsusen"}
{"id":134,"lang":"ja","text":"\"全くの無から何かの音が生まれる 無に終わるんです。それは仏教的な哲学 尹そうです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 56]","en_tr":"This piece is born within nothingness [無] and ends as nothingness. That is the Buddhist philosophy.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"無 mu"}
{"id":135,"lang":"ja","text":"東洋 の伝統音楽にこの原型があります。常に そのモデルは相対性を持っていて、一つ のものが常に中心になり、原則的にはこ うなるんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"East Asian traditional music has its original model. One element always becomes the center because this model always possesses relativity. This is how it goes, at least in principle.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"相対性 sōtaisei"}
{"id":136,"lang":"ja","text":"このようなばあい、終止音は一方からは単に楽曲の終止音としての意味ばかりでなく、旋律線の上下動における中核的な意味を持つという理由で、他方では、連続的にくり返されるべき性質の「数え唄」や「網引唄」の中には、かならずしも終止音に終らない旋律も多いという理由で(そのばあいですら旋律線の中核的意味を失わない)、終止音とよぶより中核音または単に核音とよぶ方が適当ではないだろうか。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"In cases like these, the ending note on the one hand holds meaning not only as a simple ending note to the piece, but also holds meaning as a central nucleus of upward and downward movement in the melodic line. On the other hand, among songs like \"Counting Song\" and \"Net-Pulling Song\" whose melodies tend to be repeated continuously, there are many songs with melodies that certainly do not end on the ending note (even in those cases, the ending notes do not lose the meaning of a central nucleus of the melodic line). For that reason, rather than calling them ending notes, it may be more appropriate to call them central nuclear tones or simply nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]","term":"上下動 jōgedō"}
{"id":137,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし、事実はもっと複雑であって、一方では次節にのべるような比較音楽学的な考察から、また他方では、雅楽輸入以前に起源を持ち、しかも現在多少とも面影をとどめていると考えられる、神楽歌や歌披講などの旋律にも明らかに核音の機能が認められるという事実から、声明にだけこの傾向の原因をもとめるわけにはゆかない.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 13]","en_tr":"On the one hand, from the perspective of comparative-musicological investigations that I will discuss in the next section; and also on the other hand from the fact that the function of nuclear tones is clearly recognized even in the melodies of kagura song and uta-hikō, which hold origins from before the importation of gagaku and furthermore are thought to retain a trace of these functioning nuclear tones in the present; we cannot go so far as to say that this is a tendency that seeks its origins only in vocal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [8.2]","term":"神楽 kagura"}
{"id":138,"lang":"ja","text":"ただ、そこにもちろん音楽をつくる、音楽を続けていくこと自体の秩序や軽然とした美学がなければならないわけです. そのひとつを私は東洋人として一番最初に見つけました。それが「ハウプト・トン」です。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 54)","en_tr":"However, there still needs to be its own organizing principles [自体の秩序] and polished aesthetics [整然とした美学] for making and sustaining sound. I discovered one of those principles first as an East Asian composer. That is Hauptton.","en_cite":"(Park (2024)  [2.4])","term":"整然とした美学 seizen to shita bigaku"}
{"id":139,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European [tonal] music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4, brackets added separately]","term":"調性 chōsei"}
{"id":140,"lang":"ja","text":"で 、 そ う い っ た 韓 国 の 楽 器 だ と か 歌 唱 法 を 、 そ の ま ま の 形 で 先 ⽣ は 作 品 の 中 で お 使 い に な る わ け で は な く て 、 よ り普 遍 的 な 語 法 と し て 昇 華 さ れ 、 理 論 的 な 体 系 づ け を な さ っ た わ け で す ね 。 そ し て 、そ こ か ら ⽣ ま れ た の が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の ⾻ 格 を 形 成 す る 「 ハ ウ プ ト ・ ト ン ( 主 要 ⾳ ) 」の 技 法 で あ る わ け で す ね .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"So, you do not directly use Korean instruments or singing styles in your compositions but transform them into more general grammar [普遍的な語法] and construct a theoretical framework. And an idea derived from it is your Juyo-um (Hauptton, [主要音]) technique, which structures your compositions.","en_cite":"(Park (2024)  [1.6])","term":"普遍的な語法 fuhentekina gohō"}
{"id":141,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし鎌倉・室町時代に興った能楽の譜では、この点がはなはだ不正確で、絶対音高を表示する譜面によってはとらえることが困難である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"However, in the sheet music of nō, which became prosperous in the Kamakura [1185 – 1333 CE] and Muromachi [1336 – 1573 CE] periods, the notes are extremely imprecise, and it is difficult to capture absolute pitch from what is displayed in the sheet music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.1]","term":"絶対音高 zettai ototaka"}
{"id":142,"lang":"ja","text":"ただ筝曲や尺八のような器楽には、非常に自由な旋律の跳躍が見られ、核音の支配から脱しているかのように思える.","cite":"[Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 9]","en_tr":"In instrumental music such as pieces for the koto or shakuhachi, we can see extraordinary freedom of melodic leaps, and so one may think that they have broken away from the control of their nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [6.1]","term":"旋律の跳躍 senritsu no chōyaku"}
{"id":143,"lang":"ja","text":"このようにな ります。しかし これよりももっ と動的な場合も あるし、もっと 静的な場合もあ ります。また上 昇性を持つ場合 と下行性を持つ 場合があります。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"But there are cases where it is more active or more static. Also, there are cases where it has a tendency upward and downward.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"上昇性 jōshōsei"}
{"id":144,"lang":"ja","text":"あの曲は四ヵ月ぐらいでしょうか。 あのオペラは一幕もので一時間かかる曲 なんですが、ドイツで拉致される前、そ の曲の初め十分ぐらいできていたんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 60]","en_tr":"The opera is in one act and takes about one hour to perform. Before I was kidnapped in Germany, the first 10 minutes' worth was completed.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [6.2]","term":"幕 maku"}
{"id":145,"lang":"ja","text":"大部分の箇所では互に4度音程をなすこれら核音だけが、音階の主要音であり、抑制された旋律的表現が、これら核音の微妙なピッチの上下変化をもたらしている。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"In most places, only nuclear tones that make up the interval of a fourth with each other are the chief notes of the scale. Restrained melodic expression brings subtle changes of pitch to these nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2]","term":"音程 ontei"}
{"id":146,"lang":"ja","text":"Bbは、ただの準備の音です。しかし、 このDを生ませるために長3度が生じま す。長3度は明るい音程です。それで、 暗い音から明るい音になります。という ことは、少しずつ光が入ってくるという。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"The Bb is just a tone for preparation. But, in order to create D, a major third is created. A major third is a bright interval. So, a dark tone becomes a bright tone. It is like light is peeking through little by little.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"音程 ontei"}
{"id":147,"lang":"ja","text":"まず童唄、民謡の類は、すでにわれわれの出発点であった。長唄については上に述べた通り、この核音の支配が顕著にあらわれているが、譜27は哥沢の例で、hとeとに現われた核音は、明瞭に旋律構造の骨格をなしている。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 8]","en_tr":"First, our points of departure were children's songs and folk songs. As I have said above about nagauta, nuclear tones strikingly control the melodies, but example 27 (Example 4) is an example of utazawa, and the pitches B and E clearly make up the skeleton of the melody's construction as its nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [5.2]","term":"童唄 warabeuta"}
{"id":148,"lang":"ja","text":"これはやがて明らかになるように、中国や朝鮮に見られる系統と同じものであって、いわゆるとよばれる旋法の影響が濃厚なことを現わしている.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 15]","en_tr":"This will eventually become clear, but it shows that its lineage is the same as that seen in China and Korea—in other words, its melodic construction is heavily influenced by the mode called ryo.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [9.2]","term":"呂 ryo"}
{"id":149,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 今 度 は 器 楽 曲 に 移 り ま し て 、 す べ て の 器 楽 曲 は ま ず 声 楽 から 受 け 継 い で 、 そ れ を 発 展 さ せ た も の とい っ て も い い わ け で す 。 た と え ば 「 ⽝ 等 」と い い ま し て 、 横 笛 を ⾧ く し た 形 の 韓 国 の 民 族 楽 器 が あ り ま し て 、 そ れ で 奏 さ れ る 節 回 し は 歌 唱 を 受 け 継 い だ も の で す 。そ し て 、 そ こ に は 線 的 な ⾳ 楽 の 妙 味 が ある わ け で す.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"And it also expands to instrumental music. One could say that all instrumental music is developed by continuing ideas from vocal music. For example, a flute-like instrument made with bamboo [橫笛] called Dae-gum is one of the Korean traditional instruments. Melodies played by that instrument are inherited from singing. They have their own charm of linear music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.5])","term":"器楽曲 utsuwa raku kyoku"}
{"id":150,"lang":"ja","text":"西洋人が持っていた形式観はないわけなんです。西洋音楽には曲を組み立ててゆくプロセスについてのはっきりしたモデルがあります。そしてそのモデルを越えて音楽は続いてゆかないのです。だから、東洋の感性をそういう伝統的な西洋のフォルムの考え方が支配してしまうのはとても危険なことです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"East Asian traditional music does not possess Western-style formalism. In Western music, there are clear process [プロセス] to assemble a composition based on clear models. Outside of these models, music cannot be sustained.","en_cite":"(Park (2024)  [2.3])","term":"プロセス purosesu"}
{"id":151,"lang":"ja","text":"大部分の箇所では互に4度音程をなすこれら核音だけが、音階の主要音であり、抑制された旋律的表現が、これら核音の微妙なピッチの上下変化をもたらしている。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"In most places, only nuclear tones that make up the interval of a fourth [scale degree] with each other are the chief notes of the scale. Restrained melodic expression brings subtle changes of pitch to these nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2, brackets added separately]","term":"度 do"}
{"id":152,"lang":"ja","text":"まず、装飾音です。装飾音から始めて、 だんだん揺れが大きくなって、場合によ ってはヴィヴラートが4度までいきます。 スタートする音に力を集めるために、装 飾音があるわけで、それ自体に意味はな いわけです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"Now, it is a decorative tone. Beginning from the decorative tone, the trembling grows larger and, at times, the vibrato gets as wide as a fourth [scale degree]. The decorative tone exists to concentrate on the tone's beginning, and it is meaningless by itself.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1, brackets added separately]","term":"度 do"}
{"id":153,"lang":"ja","text":"\"しかし、私の音楽が長時間緊張感を保っているということは、全くそのとおりなんです。私の音楽の根本をなしている線的な要素が、巧妙に持続性を持っており、そのナチュール自体が、持続の無限な可能性を持っているのです。たとえば能の音楽とか歌舞伎のように、何時間同じ線を聴いても絶対飽きない秘密がこれなんです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"But it is true that my pieces maintain tension for a long time. The foundation of my music, the linear element possesses a deft persistence. That \"nature\" [ナチュール] itself enables the unlimited persistence. For example, the secret of not being bored while listening to the same line for hours, like Noh [能] or Kabuki [歌舞技] is this.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"ナチュール nachūru"}
{"id":154,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし私の音楽はすべての流れ、本流も支流もすべてが一ル的なんです。一九」というのはここではちょっと当てはまりませんけれども、仮定して言葉を使うとすれば、そういうように線的な形態が同じ原則、同じ美学的な立場で流れていて、そのたくさんの流れの、一々の形態が同一性を持っているのです。しかも、それが分断的に使用されても、集めればその同一性の根源が得られるわけです。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 52)","en_tr":"But in my music, all flows are uniform, whether it is the mainstream or branch. \"Uniform\" [一元] may not be the best word. To use it here because of the lack of a better term, various lines flow through according to the same principle and aesthetic perspective, and the individual lines are in accordance with each other. In addition, even when a single line is used separately [分斷的], when combined, the uniformity emerges from them.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.1])","term":"一元 Ichigen"}
{"id":155,"lang":"ja","text":"\"しかし、私の音楽が長時間緊張感を保っているということは、全くそのとおりなんです。私の音楽の根本をなしている線的な要素が、巧妙に持続性を持っており、そのナチュール自体が、持続の無限な可能性を持っているのです。たとえば能の音楽とか歌舞伎のように、何時間同じ線を聴いても絶対飽きない秘密がこれなんです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"But it is true that my pieces maintain tension for a long time. The foundation of my music, the linear element possesses a deft persistence. That \"nature\" [ナチュール] itself enables the unlimited persistence. For example, the secret of not being bored while listening to the same line for hours, like Noh [能] or Kabuki [歌舞技] is this.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"歌舞伎 kabuki"}
{"id":156,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の 線 的 な 語 法 の も と に な っ て い る わ け で す ね 。 微 分 ⾳ 的 な 細 か い 揺 れ か ら 3 度 以 上 の シ ェ イ ク に ⾄ る よ う な 、 独 特 な 線 の 動 き は 、 韓 国 の 歌 唱 の ⽅ 法 か ら ⽣ み 出 さ れ た も の と 考 え て い い わ け で す ね .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"That underlies your linear [線的] musical language [語法]. It would be reasonable to say that the characteristic linear movements, ranging from fine microtonal tremors to tremolos wider than a third, come from the Korean singing [歌唱] style.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"揺れ yōre"}
{"id":157,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"作曲家 sakkyokka"}
{"id":158,"lang":"ja","text":"このようなばあい、終止音は一方からは単に楽曲の終止音としての意味ばかりでなく、旋律線の上下動における中核的な意味を持つという理由で、他方では、連続的にくり返されるべき性質の「数え唄」や「網引唄」の中には、かならずしも終止音に終らない旋律も多いという理由で(そのばあいですら旋律線の中核的意味を失わない)、終止音とよぶより中核音または単に核音とよぶ方が適当ではないだろうか。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"In cases like these, the ending note on the one hand holds meaning not only as a simple ending note to the piece, but also holds meaning as a central nucleus of upward and downward movement in the melodic line. On the other hand, among songs like \"Counting Song\" and \"Net-Pulling Song\" whose melodies tend to be repeated continuously, there are many songs with melodies that certainly do not end on the ending note (even in those cases, the ending notes do not lose the meaning of a central nucleus of the melodic line). For that reason, rather than calling them ending notes, it may be more appropriate to call them central nuclear tones or simply nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024)  [2.1]","term":"旋律 senritsu"}
{"id":159,"lang":"ja","text":"「ハウプト・トン」における陰と陽の相 対的な変化は、微細な時間によるとらえ 方から巨大な時間によるとらえ方までい ろいろな段階があります。そこでは瞬間 に永遠が反映され、永遠を瞬間としてつ かむことができるわけです。それが東洋人の「時」の考え方で、西 洋人の「時」の考え方と全く違うところ なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"In the case of a Hauptton, the relative change between yin and yang can be understood through various steps from micro-timing or macro-timing. In it, a moment reflects eternity, and eternity can be captured as a moment. That is the Eastern way of thinking about time (時), which is completely different from the Western conception of time.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"永遠 eien"}
{"id":160,"lang":"ja","text":"Bbは、ただの準備の音です。しかし、 このDを生ませるために長3度が生じま す。長3度は明るい音程です。それで、 暗い音から明るい音になります。という ことは、少しずつ光が入ってくるという。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"The Bb is just a tone for preparation. But, in order to create D, a major third is created. A major third is a bright interval. So, a dark tone becomes a bright tone. It is like light is peeking through little by little.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"明るい akarui"}
{"id":161,"lang":"ja","text":"このようなばあい、終止音は一方からは単に楽曲の終止音としての意味ばかりでなく、旋律線の上下動における中核的な意味を持つという理由で、他方では、連続的にくり返されるべき性質の「数え唄」や「網引唄」の中には、かならずしも終止音に終らない旋律も多いという理由で(そのばあいですら旋律線の中核的意味を失わない)、終止音とよぶより中核音または単に核音とよぶ方が適当ではないだろうか。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"In cases like these, the ending note on the one hand holds meaning not only as a simple ending note to the piece, but also holds meaning as a central nucleus of upward and downward movement in the melodic line. On the other hand, among songs like \"Counting Song\" and \"Net-Pulling Song\" whose melodies tend to be repeated continuously, there are many songs with melodies that certainly do not end on the ending note (even in those cases, the ending notes do not lose the meaning of a central nucleus of the melodic line). For that reason, rather than calling them ending notes, it may be more appropriate to call them central nuclear tones or simply nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]","term":"終止音 shūshi-on"}
{"id":162,"lang":"ja","text":"1つは旋律中の終止音それ自体の意味であり、他はこれら2つの終止音による完全4度の音程である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"One is the meaning of ending notes themselves within melodies, while the other is the interval of the perfect fourth that is based around these two ending notes.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"完全の音程 kanzen do no ontei"}
{"id":163,"lang":"ja","text":"そ し て 韓 国 に は 厳 格 な⽴ 場 を と る 雅 楽 ⾳ 楽 と は 別 に 、 宮 廷 ⾳ 楽 で も 寺 院 ⾳ 楽 で も な い 、⼀ 般 ⼤ 衆 と 上 流 社 会 が 共 有 し て き た 、 西 洋 に ⾒ ら れ る よ う な 知 識 社 会 で 楽 し ん で き た ⾳ 楽 世 界 が ま だ あ り ま す 。 そ れ か ら ま た 芸 術 歌 曲 、芸 術 民 謡 と い い ま す か 、 そ う い う も の が あ り ま す","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"In addition, there is a vernacular musical tradition in Korea that is neither court music nor ritual music, which had been enjoyed by both the commoners and the aristocrats, similar to the musical sphere you would see in Western intellectuals. In addition to A-ak, which takes a strict stance, there are Korean art songs and folk music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"宮廷⾳楽 Kyūtei yīn-Raku"}
{"id":164,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の 線 的 な 語 法 の も と に な っ て い る わ け で す ね 。 微 分 ⾳ 的 な 細 か い 揺 れ か ら 3 度 以 上 の シ ェ イ ク に ⾄ る よ う な 、 独 特 な 線 の 動 き は 、 韓 国 の 歌 唱 の ⽅ 法 か ら ⽣ み 出 さ れ た も の と 考 え て い い わ け で す ね .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"That underlies your linear [線的] musical language [語法]. It would be reasonable to say that the characteristic linear movements, ranging from fine microtonal tremors to tremolos wider than a third, come from the Korean singing [歌唱] style.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"韓国の歌唱 Kankuni no kashō"}
{"id":165,"lang":"ja","text":"核音の比較音楽学的意味については第4節でのべるが、西洋音楽一般についてはこれにあたるものを見ない。したがってヨーロッパの音楽理論の用語には、これを表現する適切な言葉がないのである。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 5]","en_tr":"I will discuss the meanings of nuclear tones in comparative musicology in section 4, but in Western music, we do not generally see things like this. Therefore, in European music theory terminology, there is no word that appropriately expresses this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3]","term":"音楽理論 ongaku riron"}
{"id":166,"lang":"ja","text":"フルート・ソロはDの音を直接スタート しないで、下からまず上がってくる。と いうと、Bの音が準備になる。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"The flute solo does not begin right on D but rises from below. Bb thus prepares it [the note D].","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"ソロ soro"}
{"id":167,"lang":"ja","text":"そ し て 韓 国 に は 厳 格 な⽴ 場 を と る 雅 楽 ⾳ 楽 と は 別 に 、 宮 廷 ⾳ 楽 で も 寺 院 ⾳ 楽 で も な い 、⼀ 般 ⼤ 衆 と 上 流 社 会 が 共 有 し て き た 、 西 洋 に ⾒ ら れ る よ う な 知 識 社 会 で 楽 し ん で き た ⾳ 楽 世 界 が ま だ あ り ま す 。 そ れ か ら ま た 芸 術 歌 曲 、芸 術 民 謡 と い い ま す か 、 そ う い う も の が あ り ま す","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"In addition, there is a vernacular musical tradition in Korea that is neither court music nor ritual music, which had been enjoyed by both the commoners and the aristocrats, similar to the musical sphere you would see in Western intellectuals. In addition to A-ak, which takes a strict stance, there are Korean art songs and folk music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"芸術歌曲 Jutsu uta kyoku"}
{"id":168,"lang":"ja","text":"う で す 。 厳 格 な 雅 楽 の ⾳ 楽 の 組 み ⽅ と 、 哲 学 的 な 内 容 と 、 そ れ か ら 流 暢 に 流 れ る 線 的 な 美 し さ を 、 た と え ば 南 道 唱 と か 歌 曲 と い っ た 形 式 の ⼀ 連 の 声 楽 が あ り ま す が 、 そ う い う と こ ろ か ら た く さ ん 学 び ま し た 。 そ こ に 、 今 度 は 線 的 な 動 き ⽅ の ⾳ 楽 的 な 理 論 を ⼤ 系 づ け ま し た.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"Yes. I learned a lot from A-ak's strict organization and philosophical content, and vocal music's smoothly flowing linear beauty, such as Namdo Chang and Gagok [가곡], or other vocal genres.Based on these, I organized my own musical theory of linear motion.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"線的な動き⽅の⾳楽的な理論 sen-tekina dōki fāng No yīn-Raku-tekina ri-ron."}
{"id":169,"lang":"ja","text":"「ハウプト・トン」における陰と陽の相 対的な変化は、微細な時間によるとらえ 方から巨大な時間によるとらえ方までい ろいろな段階があります。そこでは瞬間 に永遠が反映され、永遠を瞬間としてつ かむことができるわけです。それが東洋人の「時」の考え方で、西 洋人の「時」の考え方と全く違うところ なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"In the case of a Hauptton, the relative change between yin and yang can be understood through various steps from micro-timing or macro-timing. In it, a moment reflects eternity, and eternity can be captured as a moment. That is the Eastern way of thinking about time (時), which is completely different from the Western conception of time.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"巨大な時間 kyodaina jikan"}
{"id":170,"lang":"ja","text":"まず低い音から始まります。凸の音で、 これは暗い音なんです。無から生まれる。 実はこれはピアニッシモなんですけれど も。これは暗示です。まだ音じゃないわ けなんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"First of all, it begins with a low pitch [Example 1]. With the Bb, it is a dark tone. It emerges from nothing. Although it is in pianissimo, it is an implication [暗示]. It is not yet a tone.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"ピアニッシモ pianisshimo"}
{"id":171,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"楽 gaku"}
{"id":172,"lang":"ja","text":"この核音は、民謡よりもむしろ芸術音楽ことに能楽の謡や三味線声楽の長唄などでは非常にはっきりとした形で現われており、そのばあいの旋律は、ただある1つの核音をめぐって上下浮動するという状態である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"These nuclear tones appear extremely clearly in Japanese art music, especially in the utai of nō music and shamisen vocal music like nagauta, even more than in folk songs. The melodies in those (art music) cases have the characteristic of revolving around only one nuclear tone, and bobbing up and down around it.\" Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]. \"Utai 謡, while etymologically meaning simply \"song,\" has come to refer specifically to the vocal music of the nō 能 theater tradition. It is accompanied by a hayashi 囃子 ensemble, which consists of a few drums and a flute.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [footnote 4]","term":"三味線声楽 shamisen seigaku"}
{"id":173,"lang":"ja","text":"核音の比較音楽学的意味については第4節でのべるが、西洋音楽一般についてはこれにあたるものを見ない。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 5]","en_tr":"I will discuss the meanings of nuclear tones in comparative musicology in section 4, but in Western music, we do not generally see things like this.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3]","term":"音楽学 ongakugaku"}
{"id":174,"lang":"ja","text":"このようにな ります。しかし これよりももっ と動的な場合も あるし、もっと 静的な場合もあ ります。また上 昇性を持つ場合 と下行性を持つ 場合があります。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"But there are cases where it is more active or more static. Also, there are cases where it has a tendency upward and downward.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"下行性 shimo kudarisei"}
{"id":175,"lang":"ja","text":"そしてこと曲の主音が元来(h)であるから、hが重要な意味を持つのは当然としても、dもやはり重心がおかれているように見える。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 15]","en_tr":"And because this piece's tonic was originally banshikichō (B), it is natural that the pitch B would hold an important meaning, but the pitch D also seems to have been given a sense of importance.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [9.2]","term":"盤渉調 banshikichō (B)"}
{"id":176,"lang":"ja","text":"最悪の環境―監獄の中で書いた作品は 驚くことに喜劇的な内容でした。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 59]","en_tr":"\"The circumstances were the worst, however, the opera I completed in the prison was a comedy.\"","en_cite":"Park (2024) [6]","term":"喜劇 kigeki"}
{"id":177,"lang":"ja","text":"それにつ いては、コントラバスの四つのピッチカ ートが準備になる。だから、どこが準備 か、どこが本当の音かということも、常 に相対的なわけです。そして、この冒頭 ではDの音が「ハウプト・トン」なんで す。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"About this tone [Bb], the four pizzicati by the contrabass prepares it. Therefore, it is all relative when it comes to determining what is a tone and what prepares the tone. And in this opening, the D tone is a Hauptton.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"コントラバス kontorabasu"}
{"id":178,"lang":"ja","text":"1つ1つ例を上げるまでもなく、近世邦楽とよばれるもののうち、三味線を伴奏とする声楽は、一般にこの例と大差はない。民謡よりもはるかに明瞭な数小節にわたる1つの核音の支配は、このジャンルでは、唄であろうと浄瑠璃であろうとけっして珍しくない.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 8–9]","en_tr":"Without even bringing up examples one by one, among recent Japanese music, vocal music accompanied by the shamisen generally does not differ much from this example. It is not at all rare in these genres, whether song or jōruri, for the control of a single nuclear tone to cross a few measures much more clearly than in folk song.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [6.1]","term":"浄瑠璃 jōruri"}
{"id":179,"lang":"ja","text":"\"しかし、私の音楽が長時間緊張感を保っているということは、全くそのとおりなんです。私の音楽の根本をなしている線的な要素が、巧妙に持続性を持っており、そのナチュール自体が、持続の無限な可能性を持っているのです。たとえば能の音楽とか歌舞伎のように、何時間同じ線を聴いても絶対飽きない秘密がこれなんです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"But it is true that my pieces maintain tension for a long time. The foundation of my music, the linear element possesses a deft persistence. That \"nature\" [ナチュール] itself enables the unlimited persistence. For example, the secret of not being bored while listening to the same line for hours, like Noh [能] or Kabuki [歌舞技] is this.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.3])","term":"根本 konpon"}
{"id":180,"lang":"ja","text":"大部分の箇所では互に4度音程をなすこれら核音だけが、音階の主要音であり、抑制された旋律的表現が、これら核音の微妙なピッチの上下変化をもたらしている.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 11]","en_tr":"In most places, only nuclear tones that make up the interval of a fourth with each other are the chief notes of the scale. Restrained melodic expression brings subtle changes of pitch to these nuclear tones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [7.2]","term":"表現 hyōgen"}
{"id":181,"lang":"ja","text":"この音 には装飾音が欠けています。しかし、三 連符の頭の休符がそれにかわる働きをし ます。それに続いてメリスマ的な要素が ありますね。これはもう少し発展した「ハ ウプト・トン」のあり方なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"There is no decorative tone for this. But the first rest of the triplet substitutes its role. It is followed by a melismatic element. This is a more developed figure of a Hauptton.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"三連符 san ren fu"}
{"id":182,"lang":"ja","text":"この音 には装飾音が欠けています。しかし、三 連符の頭の休符がそれにかわる働きをし ます。それに続いてメリスマ的な要素が ありますね。これはもう少し発展した「ハ ウプト・トン」のあり方なんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"There is no decorative tone for this. But the first rest of the triplet substitutes its role. It is followed by a melismatic element. This is a more developed figure of a Hauptton.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"メリスマ(的) merisuma(-teki)"}
{"id":183,"lang":"ja","text":"それにつ いては、コントラバスの四つのピッチカ ートが準備になる。だから、どこが準備 か、どこが本当の音かということも、常 に相対的なわけです。そして、この冒頭 ではDの音が「ハウプト・トン」なんで す。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"About this tone [Bb], the four pizzicati by the contrabass prepares it. Therefore, it is all relative when it comes to determining what is a tone and what prepares the tone. And in this opening, the D tone is a Hauptton.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"ピッチカ ート pitchika-to"}
{"id":184,"lang":"ja","text":"\"全くの無から何かの音が生まれる 無に終わるんです。それは仏教的な哲学 尹そうです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 56]","en_tr":"This piece is born within nothingness [無] and ends as nothingness. That is the Buddhist philosophy.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"仏教的な哲学 bukkyōteki na tetsugaku"}
{"id":185,"lang":"ja","text":"だから、東洋の音楽はいつ始まってもいいし、いつ止めてもいいしという従来の伝統音楽の考え方で曲を書けば、そういう閉ざされた音の世界から開放されるのではないかと思います.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 53)","en_tr":"I think one would be freed from the world of enclosed tones [閉ざされた音] if one composes with the traditional East Asian way of thinking that music can begin and end at any point in time.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.4])","term":"閉ざされた音 tozasareta-on"}
{"id":186,"lang":"ja","text":"リズム・旋律法・多声性・楽器編成などあらゆる点でその他のジャンルと異なる","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 14]","en_tr":"All aspects such as rhythm, melodic system, polyphony, and instrumental organization differ from other genres.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [8.2]","term":"楽器編成 gakki hensei"}
{"id":187,"lang":"ja","text":"だから自分自身はそう考 えて曲を書いたけれども、それを切り離して聴いてほしいと思います。音楽には 全く描写的な要素はありません。また舞 台性も持っていません。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58-59]","en_tr":"Therefore, even though I composed these pieces with narratives in mind, I wish the pieces to be listened to without consideration for them. There are no depictive elements in music, and also no theatrical [舞台性] elements.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5.2]","term":"舞台性 butaisei"}
{"id":188,"lang":"ja","text":"ただ、そこにもちろん音楽をつくる、音楽を続けていくこと自体の秩序や軽然とした美学がなければならないわけです. そのひとつを私は東洋人として一番最初に見つけました。それが「ハウプト・トン」です。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 54)","en_tr":"However, there still needs to be its own organizing principles [自体の秩序] and polished aesthetics [整然とした美学] for making and sustaining sound. I discovered one of those principles first as an East Asian composer. That is Hauptton.","en_cite":"(Park (2024)  [2.4])","term":"自体の秩序 Jitai no chitsujo"}
{"id":189,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"室内楽曲 Shitsunai"}
{"id":190,"lang":"ja","text":"私の音楽はモニスティッシュです。というのは、私の音楽は複音楽的じゃないし、多応的な音楽ではありません。たとえばアロイス・ツインマーマン、彼のは多元的な音楽ですね。根源が違っている音楽的な要素が同時に流れて秩序を保ちつつ、対立しながら、ついにはそれらが和合して、皆楽的な大きな向上をするというものです.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese 52)","en_tr":"My music is monistic (monistisch). My music is not polyphonic or pluralistic. For example, Bernd Alois Zimmermann's music is pluralistic. Elements from different roots flow together, maintain order, oppose, but ultimately come together to greatly elevate the music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [2.1])","term":"多応的 ta yīng mato "}
{"id":191,"lang":"ja","text":"また1つの核音の支配圏から脱して他の核音の圏に移るには、それだけの旋律構成上の力がなければならない。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 6]","en_tr":"Also, in order to escape one nuclear tone's sphere of control and move to another nuclear tone's sphere, the melody must be strongly constructed [melodic construction].","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [3, brackets added separately]","term":"旋律構成 senritsu kōsei"}
{"id":192,"lang":"ja","text":"純粋な音自体を持って、人間の現世を超越した、そういう人間世界と天空の世界の中間、人間世界と天空の世界の接触といいますか、あるいは地 獄のというように、全く人間の現世の世 界とは離れて、超越した宇宙の問題を取 り扱った、そういう作品は他にもたくさ んあります。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 59]","en_tr":"The realm that is in between the mortal world and the celestial world, or perhaps a contact between the two worlds. There are many other compositions that deal with a topic that is separate from the real world, such as purgatory and a transcendent universe.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5.3]","term":"天空の世界 tenkū no sekai"}
{"id":193,"lang":"ja","text":"この例では小節の縦線は省いておいたが、上・下段のアナリーゼによる縦線と、小節の縦線とはある点では三者共に一致する。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"In this example, I have omitted the bar lines, but the vertical lines based on the analyses above and below the notation, to a certain point, agree with where the bar lines would be.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.2]","term":"小節の縦線 kobushi no tatesen"}
{"id":194,"lang":"ja","text":"譜32は、古いもののうちでもとくに有名な雅楽の<青海波>から竜笛の旋律だけを抜きだしたものである.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 14]","en_tr":"Example 32 extracts only the ryūteki melody from \"Seigaiha,\" a gagaku piece that is especially famous among the older ones.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [9.1]","term":" 龍笛 ryūteki"}
{"id":195,"lang":"ja","text":"この核音は、民謡よりもむしろ芸術音楽ことに能楽の謡や三味線声楽の長唄などでは非常にはっきりとした形で現われており、そのばあいの旋律は、ただある1つの核音をめぐって上下浮動するという状態である。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 3]","en_tr":"These nuclear tones appear extremely clearly in Japanese art music, especially in the utai of nō music and shamisen vocal music like nagauta, even more than in folk songs. The melodies in those (art music) cases have the characteristic of revolving around only one nuclear tone, and bobbing up and down around it.\" Hynes-Tawa (2024) [2.1]. \"Utai 謡, while etymologically meaning simply \"song,\" has come to refer specifically to the vocal music of the nō 能 theater tradition. It is accompanied by a hayashi 囃子 ensemble, which consists of a few drums and a flute.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [footnote 4]","term":"謡 utai"}
{"id":196,"lang":"ja","text":"譜30、31はそれぞれ天台および真言の声明の例であるが、どちらも上下動の少い、どちらかといえば単調な旋律である.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 12]","en_tr":"Examples 30 and 31 are examples of Tendai and Shingon chant respectively, but microtonal fluctuation is little in both, and both have simple melodies.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [8.1]","term":"声明 seimei/shōmyō"}
{"id":197,"lang":"ja","text":"「時」の考え方が形式観に反映した 例として西洋ではソナタ形式があります が、ソナタ形式ですと、第一主題部があ り、第二主題部がある。これらは対立し た区間であり、第二主題の部分は第一主 題と異なった時間を独自に形成するわけ ですから、瞬間に世界を持つ陰陽とは全 く異なるということですね。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"The Sonata form might be one example that reflects the Western formalistic view of time. In Sonata form, there are primary and secondary theme areas. They are contrasting sections that independently develop [the sense of] time. Therefore, it is completely different from yin and yang, which contain an eternity in a moment.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.2]","term":"第二主題部 dai ni shudaibu"}
{"id":198,"lang":"ja","text":"そ れ が 、 先 ⽣ の 作 品 の 線 的 な 語 法 の も と に な っ て い る わ け で す ね 。 微 分 ⾳ 的 な 細 か い 揺 れ か ら 3 度 以 上 の シ ェ イ ク に ⾄ る よ う な 、 独 特 な 線 の 動 き は 、 韓 国 の 歌 唱 の ⽅ 法 か ら ⽣ み 出 さ れ た も の と 考 え て い い わ け で す ね .","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"That underlies your linear [線的] musical language [語法]. It would be reasonable to say that the characteristic linear movements, ranging from fine microtonal tremors to tremolos wider than a third, come from the Korean singing [歌唱] style.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.4])","term":"線的語法 sen-teki gohō"}
{"id":199,"lang":"ja","text":"そ し て 韓 国 に は 厳 格 な⽴ 場 を と る 雅 楽 ⾳ 楽 と は 別 に 、 宮 廷 ⾳ 楽 で も 寺 院 ⾳ 楽 で も な い 、⼀ 般 ⼤ 衆 と 上 流 社 会 が 共 有 し て き た 、 西 洋 に ⾒ ら れ る よ う な 知 識 社 会 で 楽 し ん で き た ⾳ 楽 世 界 が ま だ あ り ま す 。 そ れ か ら ま た 芸 術 歌 曲 、芸 術 民 謡 と い い ま す か 、 そ う い う も の が あ り ま す","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"In addition, there is a vernacular musical tradition in Korea that is neither court music nor ritual music, which had been enjoyed by both the commoners and the aristocrats, similar to the musical sphere you would see in Western intellectuals. In addition to A-ak, which takes a strict stance, there are Korean art songs and folk music.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"芸術民謡 Jutsu Min Utai"}
{"id":200,"lang":"ja","text":"これは笛であるため、音程の跳躍がはなはだしいが、それを筝曲のばあいのように、オクターヴを同音と考えて見ると、案外旋律的な動きとなる.","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 14]","en_tr":"Because this melody is for a flute, the intervallic leaps are extreme, but as in the case with koto music, if you think of octaves as equivalent, its movement becomes surprisingly conjunct.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [9.2]","term":"同音 dōon"}
{"id":201,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1]","term":"音楽 ongaku"}
{"id":202,"lang":"ja","text":"このどちらもが、日本の音階と旋律法のヨーロッパとの違いはもちろん、アジア音楽の中での、特異性をきわめて明確に規定する要素なのであるが、ここではまず前者について考えて見よう。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 1]","en_tr":"For both of these, the differences between Japanese musical [melodic] rules and those of Europe are of course the elements make Asian music seem so extremely peculiar.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [1.1, brackets added separately]","term":"旋律法 senritsuhō"}
{"id":203,"lang":"ja","text":"自分で音楽を考え る、ファンタジーをつかむという自由だ けがそこにあったのです。身体的な条件 は極度に悪くても、そのファンタジーを つかむ自由はありました。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 60]","en_tr":"There existed only freedom to think about my music and to unfold my fantasy. Even though my physical condition was extremely poor, I had the freedom to unfold fantasy.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [6.3]","term":"ファンタジー fantajī"}
{"id":204,"lang":"ja","text":"高い意味での純粋性―全ての不条理を 克服してそこに純粋性を見出す。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 58]","en_tr":"Purity comes from overcoming the contradiction within the whole.\"","en_cite":"Park (2024) [5]","term":"純粋性 junsuisei"}
{"id":205,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European [tonal] music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4, brackets added separately]","term":"伝統音楽 dentō ongaku"}
{"id":206,"lang":"ja","text":"東洋 の伝統音楽にこの原型があります。常に そのモデルは相対性を持っていて、一つ のものが常に中心になり、原則的にはこ うなるんです。","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"East Asian traditional music has its original model. One element always becomes the center because this model always possesses relativity. This is how it goes, at least in principle.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"伝統音楽 dentō ongaku"}
{"id":207,"lang":"ja","text":"これはヨーロッパの調性音楽が、次第に従来の長・短調組織からぬけだして、自由な音語を使うようになってから、もっともひろい意味での調性の中心になる音という意味に使われていたものを、伝統音楽のばあいに適用したものと解することができる。","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 7]","en_tr":"It is understood that Mr. Itō applied the word \"central tone\" as something commonly used in Japanese traditional music, in the same way European music used it in a free pitch language after it gradually began to pull away from its original major- and minor-key organization of tonal music.","en_cite":"Hynes-Tawa (2024) [4]","term":"長・短調組織 chō tanchō soshiki"}
{"id":208,"lang":"ja","text":"先生の作品表を拝見いたしますと、オペラ、管弦楽曲、室内楽曲、声楽曲と、膨大な数に上っているわけですけれども、それらの作品はいわゆる西洋楽器、それから西洋の形態でつくられているものがすべてのように思います。われわれ日本の作曲家は邦楽器を用いることも多いのですが、先生は韓国の伝統楽器、あるいは東アジアの伝統楽器のための作品をお書きになったことはないのですか。","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 50)","en_tr":"When looking at your list of compositions, I find numerous operas, orchestral music, chamber pieces, vocal pieces, and so on, but they all seem to be composed for so-called \"Western\" instruments and in \"Western\" configuration. For Japanese composers, there are some compositions written for Japanese traditional instruments. Have you composed a piece for traditional Korean instruments?","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.1])","term":"作品表を Sakuhin-hyō"}
{"id":209,"lang":"ja","text":"しかし、この旋律が順次進行を主体とする声楽と本質的にちがった種類のものではなく","cite":"Koizumi Fumio (1958) [p. 9]","en_tr":"However, this melody is not essentially different from vocal melodies that make most of their material from conjunct motion.","en_cite":"[Hynes-Tawa (2024) [6.2]","term":"順次進行 junjishinkō"}
{"id":210,"lang":"ja","text":"そ の ひ と つ に 、 南 道 唱 と い いま し て 、 南 韓 国 あ た り を 中 ⼼ と し て 発 展し た 朗 々 と 歌 う 民 族 ⾳ 楽 が あ り ま す 。 そこ か ら 私 は と て も 影 響 を 受 け ま し た.","cite":"(Yun (1984) - Japanese, 51)","en_tr":"One of them is called Namdo Chang [남도창, 南道唱], which is folk music that features a clear and loud voice and has been passed down in the southern Korean region. I have been greatly influenced by that genre.","en_cite":"(Park (2024) [1.3])","term":"南道唱 Minami Michi chàng"}
{"id":211,"lang":"ja","text":"また「ハウプト・トン」は断続的に切れ切れの形で現れることもあります。と もかく様々な線となって現れますが…","cite":"Yun (1984) - Japanese [p. 57]","en_tr":"Also, a Hauptton sometimes intermittently appears in the shape of little pieces. In any case, it appears as various lines.","en_cite":"Park (2024) [4.1]","term":"線 sen"}
{"id":212,"lang":"es","text":"La diferencia fundamental entre estos procedimientos y los de mis \"Leyes de metamorfosis\" consiste en que en los ejemplos que he citado de los más eminentes maestros clásicos se alteran las melodías con sonidos que no contiene el original, y en mis \"Leyes de metamorfosis\" no se agrega ni se quita ni una sola nota de las que escribieron los autores, y eso no sólo en su parte melódica, sino también en la armónica y en la rítmica. En la rítmica y la melódica hay todo un mundo de posibilidades jamás presentidas antes de la revolución del Sonido 13.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.20]","en_tr":"The fundamental difference between these procedures and those of my \"Laws of Metamorphosis\" is that in the examples I have cited by the most eminent classical maestros, melodies are altered with sounds not contained in the original. In my \"Laws of Metamorphosis,\" not a single note is added or removed from what the author wrote originally, neither in its melodic aspect, nor even in its harmonic and rhythmic aspects. In the rhythmic and melodic domains there is a whole world of possibilities never anticipated before the revolution of Sonido 13.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.20]","term":"Nota"}
{"id":213,"lang":"es","text":"La llamada escala cromática, y que en su forma clásica procede por semitonos, en su metamorfosis al duplo quedará por tonos enteros.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.18]","en_tr":"The so-called chromatic scale, which in its classical form proceeds by semitones, proceeds by whole tones under its metamorphosis to the double.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.18]","term":"Tonos enteros"}
{"id":214,"lang":"es","text":"Podrían incluirse, si acaso, en el campo de las metamorfosis, las imitaciones por movimiento contrario, pues éstas, aunque no alteran las relaciones de los intervalos, son, sin embargo, diferentes del tema que imitan.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.5]","en_tr":"Imitations by contrary motion could perhaps be included within the domain of metamorphosis, because although they do not alter intervallic relationships, they nevertheless differ from the themes they imitate.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.5]","term":"Movimiento contrario"}
{"id":215,"lang":"es","text":"Si dentro de la moderna mentalidad quisiéramos encontrar un sinónimo para estas \"Leyes de metamorfosis\", paréceme que nada sería tan a propósito como llamarlas \"Leyes de relaciones y proporciones,\" pues efectivamente descansan sobre las relaciones y proporciones de los intervalos, tanto en su parte melódica como en la armónica.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.15]","en_tr":"If we wanted to find a synonym for these \"Laws of Metamorphosis\" from a modern point of view, I think nothing would be more appropriate than \"Laws of Relations and Proportions.\" Ultimately, these laws rest on intervallic relations and proportions in both their melodic and harmonic aspects.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.15]","term":"Proporciones"}
{"id":216,"lang":"es","text":"Como las ocho octavas al metamorfosearse al duplo necesitarían dieciséis octavas de extensión, se tendrá cuidado en composiciones metamorfoseadas al duplo y que en el original excedan de cuatro octavas, por la parte grave y la aguda, de invertir las notas que excedan de la extensión del piano, ya sea bajándolas o subiéndolas según el cas…","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.8]","en_tr":"When metamorphosed to the double, eight octaves necessitate a range of sixteen octaves. When original compositions exceed four octaves, then, care must be taken to invert the notes that lie outside the range of the piano, either by lowering them or raising them, depending on the case.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.8]","term":"Octavas"}
{"id":217,"lang":"es","text":"No conozco ningún ejemplo en el cual se hayan operado modificaciones melódicas, armónicas y rítmicas, sin alterar los modelos, y con mi \"Ley de metamorfosis\" pueden efectuarse cambios en la melodía, en la armonía y el ritmo, sin agregar ni suprimir ni una sola nota.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3]","en_tr":"I do not know any example in which melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic modifications have been used without altering the models. With my \"Law of Metamorphosis,\" changes in melody, harmony, and rhythm can be carried out without adding or removing a single note.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3]","term":"Modificaciones rítmicas"}
{"id":218,"lang":"es","text":"Existe en el clasicismo musical algo que pudiera creerse relacionado con estas \"Leyes de Metamorfosis\": los procedimientos por \"aumentación\" y \"disminución,\" que se emplean en el canon y la fuga, pero debe desecharse tal idea; pues positivamente no tienen semejanza con lo que constituye la base misma de mis \"Leyes de metamorfosis.\"","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.3]","en_tr":"In classical music, there exist procedures that could be thought of as related to these \"Laws of Metamorphosis\": the procedures of \"augmentation\" and \"diminution\" that are employed in canon and fugue. But such a notion must be discarded, because augmentation and diminution bear absolutely no relationship to the very foundation of my \"Laws of Metamorphosis.\"","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.3]","term":"Aumentación"}
{"id":219,"lang":"es","text":"pero [el canon] afectaba únicamente la velocidad o la lentitud de un tema, haciendo más aprisa o más despacio una melodía, lo que nada tenía en el fondo que pudiera sugerir la metamorfosis como yo la entiendo: pues la modificación era fácilmente reconocible","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.4] (See also Canon)","en_tr":"But canon affected only the speed or the length of a theme, made a melody quicker or slower, without having anything at its basis that could suggest metamorphosis as I understand it. Its modification was easily recognizable.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.4]","term":"Melodía"}
{"id":220,"lang":"es","text":"En cuanto al perfecto menor, que tiene sobre el bajo un intervalo de tres semitonos, y sobre la nota alta de éste, uno de cuatro, tendrá al metamorfosearse al duplo, uno de seis semitonos sobre el bajo, en vez de tres, y sobre la nota alta de éste, uno de ocho semitonos en vez de cuatro.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.8]","en_tr":"The minor triad has an interval of three semitones above the bass, and above that, an interval of four semitones. Under metamorphosis to the double, the first interval will reach six semitones above the bass, and the second, another eight semitones.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.8]","term":"Semitono/medio tono"}
{"id":221,"lang":"es","text":"Existe en el clasicismo musical algo que pudiera creerse relacionado con estas \"Leyes de Metamorfosis\": los procedimientos por \"aumentación\" y \"disminución,\" que se emplean en el canon y la fuga, pero debe desecharse tal idea; pues positivamente no tienen semejanza con lo que constituye la base misma de mis \"Leyes de metamorfosis.\"","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.3]","en_tr":"In classical music, there exist procedures that could be thought of as related to these \"Laws of Metamorphosis\": the procedures of \"augmentation\" and \"diminution\" that are employed in canon and fugue. But such a notion must be discarded, because augmentation and diminution bear absolutely no relationship to the very foundation of my \"Laws of Metamorphosis.\"","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.3]","term":"Disminución"}
{"id":222,"lang":"es","text":"He aquí esta obra escrita originalmente en cuartos, octavos y dieciséisavos de tono, para los solistas.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.12]","en_tr":"Here is that work, written originally in quarter tones, eighth tones, and sixteenth tones for the soloists.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.12]]","term":"Cuartos de tono"}
{"id":223,"lang":"es","text":"Como las ocho octavas al metamorfosearse al duplo necesitarían dieciséis octavas de extensión, se tendrá cuidado en composiciones metamorfoseadas al duplo y que en el original excedan de cuatro octavas, por la parte grave y la aguda, de invertir las notas que excedan de la extensión del piano, ya sea bajándolas o subiéndolas según el caso, pero aprovechando para ello los intervalos largos para que la inversión se note lo menos posible.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.8]","en_tr":"When metamorphosed to the double, eight octaves necessitate a range of sixteen octaves. When original compositions exceed four octaves, then, care must be taken to invert the notes that lie outside the range of the piano, either by lowering them or raising them, depending on the case. Here, one should make use of large intervals, so that this inversion is noticed as little as possible.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.8]","term":"Inversión"}
{"id":224,"lang":"es","text":"y con mi \"Ley de metamorfosis\" pueden efectuarse cambios en la melodía, en la armonía y el ritmo, sin agregar ni suprimir ni una sola nota.","cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3])","en_tr":"With my \"Law of Metamorphosis,\" changes in melody, harmony, and rhythm can be carried out without adding or removing a single note.","en_cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3])","term":"Ritmo"}
{"id":225,"lang":"es","text":"Las notas marcadas con asteriscos son adornos al mismo tema.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.10]","en_tr":"The notes marked with asterisks are ornaments on the same theme.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.10]","term":"Adornos"}
{"id":226,"lang":"es","text":"Desde antes de Juan Sebastián Bach, existía ya el canon por \"aumentación\" y \"disminución,\" pero afectaba únicamente la velocidad o la lentitud de un tema, haciendo más aprisa o más despacio una melodía, lo que nada tenía en el fondo que pudiera sugerir la metamorfosis como yo la entiendo: pues la modificación era fácilmente reconocible.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.4]","en_tr":"Since before Johann Sebastian Bach, there already existed canon by \"augmentation\" and \"diminution.\" But canon affected only the speed or the length of a theme, made a melody quicker or slower, without having anything at its basis that could suggest metamorphosis as I understand it. Its modification was easily recognizable.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.4]","term":"Canon"}
{"id":227,"lang":"es","text":"He aquí esta obra escrita originalmente en cuartos, octavos y dieciséisavos de tono, para los solistas.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.12]","en_tr":"Here is that work, written originally in quarter tones, eighth tones, and sixteenth tones for the soloists.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.12]","term":"Dieciséisavos de tono"}
{"id":228,"lang":"es","text":"…acompañara a base de semitonos en el cual los intervalos de 4os. de tono se ampliaron a semitonos.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.13]","en_tr":"…accompanied [my soloists] in twelve-tone equal temperament, in such a way that quarter-tone intervals were expanded to become semitones.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.13]","term":"Base de semitonos (?)"}
{"id":229,"lang":"es","text":"…es decir, que así como en el ejemplo 44 se conservó el Do como tónica, se vayan conservando en cada caso las tónicas respectivas; aunque no hay razón alguna en contra de quien prefiera servirse únicamente de la clave que indico para Do mayor, pero en ese caso no se conservarán las tónicas. Si se conserva inamovible únicamente la nota Do para todas las tonalidades, la impresión no será la misma que si se conservara en cada caso la tónica de la obra metamorfoseada.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.7]","en_tr":"In other words, just as C was preserved as tonic in Example 44, other tonics can be preserved. Although there is no reason not to work solely with the guide I indicate for C major, in that case, one will not be preserving tonics. When one holds C fixed for all tonalities, the impression will not be the same as when one preserves, in each instance, the tonic of the metamorphosed work.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.7]","term":"Tónica"}
{"id":230,"lang":"es","text":"Las metamorfosis presentadas en las escalas que anteceden son todas al duplo, lo que significa que donde hay un intervalo de tono se escribirán dos tonos; que donde hay uno y medio se escribirán tres, y que donde hay dos se escribirán cuatro, que donde hay un semitono se escribirá un tono, etc..","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.16]","en_tr":"The metamorphoses presented in the previous scales are all doublings, which means that where there is an interval of a whole tone, two whole tones are written; where there are three semitones, three whole tones are written; where there are two whole tones, four whole tones are written; where there is one semitone, one whole tone is written; etc.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.16]","term":"Duplo"}
{"id":231,"lang":"es","text":"He aquí la escala menor armónica, metamorfoseada.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.13]","en_tr":"Here is the harmonic minor scale, metamorphosed…","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.13]","term":"Escala menor armónica"}
{"id":232,"lang":"es","text":"pero [el canon] afectaba únicamente la velocidad o la lentitud de un tema, haciendo más aprisa o más despacio una melodía, lo que nada tenía en el fondo que pudiera sugerir la metamorfosis como yo la entiendo: pues la modificación era fácilmente reconocible","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.4](See also Canon)","en_tr":"But canon affected only the speed or the length of a theme, made a melody quicker or slower, without having anything at its basis that could suggest metamorphosis as I understand it. Its modification was easily recognizable.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.4]","term":"Tema"}
{"id":233,"lang":"es","text":"En el sentido idiomático, \"metamórfosis\" o \"metamorfosis\" significa transformar una cosa en otra. Por esta causa adopté tal término para designar las transformaciones melódicas, armónicas y rítmicas, a que pueden someterse las composiciones musicales.\" Cannon-Brown (2024) [p. 14-15]. \"…con mi \"Ley de metamorfosis\" pueden efectuarse cambios en la melodía, en la armonía y el ritmo, sin agregar ni suprimir ni una sola nota.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.1]","en_tr":"In its idiomatic sense, \"metamorphosis\" means the transformation of one thing into another. I adopt the term in this way to designate the melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic transformations to which musical compositions can be subjected.\" Cannon-Brown (2024) [p. 14-15]. \"With my \"Law of Metamorphosis,\" changes in melody, harmony, and rhythm can be carried out without adding or removing a single note.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.1]","term":"Metamórfosis"}
{"id":234,"lang":"es","text":"Tal ampliación sólo será posible si el oído humano logra oír y distinguir claramente sonidos producidos por 131,072 vibraciones en un segundo.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.9]","en_tr":"Such an expanded musical range will be possible only if the human ear manages to hear, and to distinguish clearly, sounds produced at 131,072 cycles per second.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.9]","term":"Sonido"}
{"id":235,"lang":"es","text":"…Ofrenda musical y su Arte de la fuga, las maravillas más estupendas que produjo el clasicismo en los campos de la técnica musical del sistema de los 12 sonidos.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.8]","en_tr":"…Musical Offering and his Art of the Fugue, the greatest wonders classicism produced under the musical techniques of the twelve-note musical system.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.8]","term":"Sonido"}
{"id":236,"lang":"es","text":"…y en mis \"Leyes de metamorfosis\" no se agrega ni se quita ni una sola nota de las que escribieron los autores, y eso no sólo en su parte melódica, sino también en la armónica y en la rítmica. En la rítmica y la melódica hay todo un mundo de posibilidades jamás presentidas antes de la revolución del Sonido 13.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.20]","en_tr":"In my \"Laws of Metamorphosis,\" not a single note is added or removed from what the author wrote originally, neither in its melodic aspect, nor even in its harmonic and rhythmic aspects. In the rhythmic and melodic domains there is a whole world of possibilities never anticipated before the revolution of Sonido 13.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.20]","term":"Revolución musical del “Sonido 13”"}
{"id":237,"lang":"es","text":"Existe en el clasicismo musical algo que pudiera creerse relacionado con estas \"Leyes de Metamorfosis\": los procedimientos por \"aumentación\" y \"disminución,\" que se emplean en el canon y la fuga, pero debe desecharse tal idea; pues positivamente no tienen semejanza con lo que constituye la base misma de mis \"Leyes de metamorfosis.\" Son éstas de tal magnitud y las transformaciones que efectúan tan fundamentales, que estoy absolutamente seguro de que ningún compositor, por grandes que sean sus conocimientos en materia musical, podrá reconocer sus propias composiciones al oírlas, una vez que se les hayan aplicado las leyes que aquí expongo.","cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.3])","en_tr":"In classical music, there exist procedures that could be thought of as related to these \"Laws of Metamorphosis\": the procedures of \"augmentation\" and \"diminution\" that are employed in canon and fugue. But such a notion must be discarded, because augmentation and diminution bear absolutely no relationship to the very foundation of my \"Laws of Metamorphosis.\" These Laws are of such magnitude, and the transformations they effect are so fundamental, that I am absolutely sure no composer, however great their knowledge of musical matters, will be able to recognize their own compositions aurally once subjected to the laws I present here.","en_cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.3])","term":"Leyes"}
{"id":238,"lang":"es","text":"No conozco ningún ejemplo en el cual se hayan operado modificaciones melódicas, armónicas y rítmicas, sin alterar los modelos, y con mi \"Ley de metamorfosis\" pueden efectuarse cambios en la melodía, en la armonía y el ritmo, sin agregar ni suprimir ni una sola nota.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3]","en_tr":"I do not know any example in which melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic modifications have been used without altering the models. With my \"Law of Metamorphosis,\" changes in melody, harmony, and rhythm can be carried out without adding or removing a single note.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3]","term":"Modificaciones armónicas"}
{"id":239,"lang":"es","text":"He aquí esta obra escrita originalmente en cuartos, octavos y dieciséisavos de tono, para los solistas.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.12]","en_tr":"Here is that work, written originally in quarter tones, eighth tones, and sixteenth tones for the soloists.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [4.12]","term":"Octavos de tono"}
{"id":240,"lang":"es","text":"No conozco ningún ejemplo en el cual se hayan operado modificaciones melódicas, armónicas y rítmicas, sin alterar los modelos, y con mi \"Ley de metamorfosis\" pueden efectuarse cambios en la melodía, en la armonía y el ritmo, sin agregar ni suprimir ni una sola nota.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3]","en_tr":"I do not know any example in which melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic modifications have been used without altering the models. With my \"Law of Metamorphosis,\" changes in melody, harmony, and rhythm can be carried out without adding or removing a single note.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.3]","term":"Modificaciones melódicas"}
{"id":241,"lang":"es","text":"He aquí la llamada escala menor melódica, metamorfoseada al duplo.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.11]","en_tr":"Here is the so-called melodic minor scale, metamorphosed to the double.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.11]","term":"Escala menor melódica"}
{"id":242,"lang":"es","text":"Podrían incluirse, si acaso, en el campo de las metamorfosis, las imitaciones por movimiento contrario, pues éstas, aunque no alteran las relaciones de los intervalos, son, sin embargo, diferentes del tema que imitan.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.5]","en_tr":"Imitations by contrary motion could perhaps be included within the domain of metamorphosis, because although they do not alter intervallic relationships, they nevertheless differ from the themes they imitate.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.5]","term":"Imitaciones"}
{"id":243,"lang":"es","text":"as metamorfosis presentadas en las escalas que anteceden son todas al duplo, lo que significa que donde hay un intervalo de tono se escribirán dos tonos; que donde hay uno y medio se escribirán tres, y que donde hay dos se escribirán cuatro, que donde hay un semitono se escribirá un tono, etc.","cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.16])","en_tr":"The metamorphoses presented in the previous scales are all doublings, which means that where there is an interval of a whole tone, two whole tones are written; where there are three semitones, three whole tones are written; where there are two whole tones, four whole tones are written; where there is one semitone, one whole tone is written; etc.","en_cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.16])","term":"Tono"}
{"id":244,"lang":"es","text":"Con lo visto será bastante para comprender que, como en la llamada escala diatónica mayor, hay del primer grado al segundo un tono; al metamorfosearse al duplo, habrá dos; y como del segundo grado al tercero de la escala diatónica hay también un tono, con la metamorfosis al duplo habrá del segundo grado al tercero dos tonos; del tercero al cuarto grados hay un semitono, y es evidente que al metamorfosearse al duplo habrá del tercer grado al cuarto un tono en vez de un semitono, etc.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.16]","en_tr":"This suffices to show how in the so-called diatonic major scale, there is a whole tone between the first and second scale degrees, which, when metamorphosed to the double, becomes two whole tones; how between the second and third degrees of the diatonic scale, a whole tone becomes two whole tones; how between the third and fourth degrees, a semitone becomes a whole tone; etc.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.16]","term":"Escala diatónica mayor"}
{"id":245,"lang":"es","text":"…o sea que la mentalidad de los compositores estaba dominada por la idea de escribir temas con variaciones, idea absolutamente excluída de mis Leyes, pues la característica de ellas es que jamás se agrega ni suprime ninguna nota a las composiciones originales metamorfoseadas.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.2]","en_tr":"Composers' thinking has been dominated by the idea of writing themes and variations, an idea absolutely excluded from my Laws, because their defining characteristic is that no note is ever added or removed from compositions that are metamorphosed.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.2]","term":"Temas con variaciones"}
{"id":246,"lang":"es","text":"Muy conocido es, igualmente, el efecto formidable logrado por Ricardo Wagner en la obertura de Tannhauser, en la cual la aumentación rítmica y el cambio de matiz dan carácter de apoteosis al tema místico en el final de dicha Obra.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.21]","en_tr":"Equally well-known is the formidable effect achieved by Richard Wagner in the overture to Tannhäuser, in which rhythmic augmentation and shifting nuances lend a character of apotheosis to the mystical theme at the end of the work.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.21]]","term":"Apoteosis"}
{"id":247,"lang":"es","text":"Ejemplos de este género se encuentran a menudo en las obras de Bach, especialmente en su Ofrenda musical y su Arte de la fuga, las maravillas más estupendas que produjo el clasicismo en los campos de la técnica musical del sistema de los 12 sonidos.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.8]","en_tr":"Examples of this kind are often encountered in the works of Bach, especially in his Musical Offering and his Art of the Fugue, the greatest wonders classicism produced under the musical techniques of the twelve-note musical system.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.8]","term":"Fuga"}
{"id":248,"lang":"es","text":"Podrían incluirse, si acaso, en el campo de las metamorfosis, las imitaciones por movimiento contrario, pues éstas, aunque no alteran las relaciones de los intervalos, son, sin embargo, diferentes del tema que imitan.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.5]","en_tr":"Imitations by contrary motion could perhaps be included within the domain of metamorphosis, because although they do not alter intervallic relationships, they nevertheless differ from the themes they imitate.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.5]","term":"Relaciones de los intervalos"}
{"id":249,"lang":"es","text":"Ejemplos de este género se encuentran a menudo en las obras de Bach, especialmente en su Ofrenda musical y su Arte de la fuga, las maravillas más estupendas que produjo el clasicismo en los campos de la técnica musical del sistema de los 12 sonidos.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.8]","en_tr":"Examples of this kind are often encountered in the works of Bach, especially in his Musical Offering and his Art of the Fugue, the greatest wonders classicism produced under the musical techniques of the twelve-note musical system.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.8]","term":"Sistema de los 12 sonidos"}
{"id":250,"lang":"es","text":"…o sea que la mentalidad de los compositores estaba dominada por la idea de escribir temas con variaciones, idea absolutamente excluída de mis Leyes, pues la característica de ellas es que jamás se agrega ni suprime ninguna nota a las composiciones originales metamorfoseadas.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.2]","en_tr":"Composers' thinking has been dominated by the idea of writing themes and variations, an idea absolutely excluded from my Laws, because their defining characteristic is that no note is ever added or removed from compositions that are metamorphosed.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.2]","term":"Compositor"}
{"id":251,"lang":"es","text":"En cuanto al perfecto menor, que tiene sobre el bajo un intervalo de tres semitonos, y sobre la nota alta de éste, uno de cuatro, tendrá al metamorfosearse al duplo, uno de seis semitonos sobre el bajo, en vez de tres, y sobre la nota alta de éste, uno de ocho semitonos en vez de cuatro.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.8]","en_tr":"The minor triad has an interval of three semitones above the bass, and above that, an interval of four semitones. Under metamorphosis to the double, the first interval will reach six semitones above the bass, and the second, another eight semitones.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.8]","term":"Acorde perfecto menor"}
{"id":252,"lang":"es","text":"Fáltanos el acorde aumentado. Como este acorde contiene dos intervalos de cuatro semitonos, al metamorfosearse al duplo tendrá dos de ocho semitonos.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.13]","en_tr":"At last, we come to the augmented triad. As this chord contains two intervals of four semitones, it will have two intervals of eight semitones under metamorphosis to the double.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.13]","term":"Acorde aumentado"}
{"id":253,"lang":"es","text":"El disminuido, que tiene dos intervalos de tres semitonos, tendrá al metamorfosearse al duplo dos seis semitonos, y el resultado final será.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.11]","en_tr":"The diminished triad, which has two intervals of three semitones, will have two intervals of six semitones when metamorphosed to the double, and the final result will be the following.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.11]","term":"Acorde disminuído"}
{"id":254,"lang":"es","text":"Tal cosa significa que como el acorde perfecto mayor, por ejemplo, se obtiene contando del bajo hacia arriba, un intervalo de cuatro semitonos, y sobre la nota superior de éste, otro de tres semitonos, al metamorfosearse al duplo, en vez del intervalo de cuatro semitonos sobre el bajo, se escribirá uno de ocho, y sobre la nota de éste, en vez de uno de tres, irá uno de seis. De lo dicho se desprende que el acorde perfecto mayor…metamorfoseado al duplo, quedará así:","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.4]","en_tr":"Take, for example, the major triad, which is obtained by counting an interval of four semitones above the bass, followed by another interval three semitones above that. Under metamorphosis to the double, instead of counting an interval of four semitones above the bass, we will count eight, and instead of counting three semitones above that note, we will count six. It follows that for a major triad…when metamorphosed to the double, will look like this:","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [3.4]","term":"Acorde perfecto mayor"}
{"id":255,"lang":"es","text":"La llamada escala cromática, y que en su forma clásica procede por semitonos, en su metamorfosis al duplo quedará por tonos enteros.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.18]","en_tr":"The so-called chromatic scale, which in its classical form proceeds by semitones, proceeds by whole tones under its metamorphosis to the double.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.18]","term":"Escala cromática"}
{"id":256,"lang":"es","text":"Por esta causa adopté tal término [metamórfosis] para designar las transformaciones melódicas, armónicas y rítmicas, a que pueden someterse las composiciones musicales.","cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.1] (See also Metamórfosis)","en_tr":"I adopt the term in this way to designate the melodic, harmonic, and rhythmic transformations to which musical compositions can be subjected.","en_cite":"Cannon-Brown (2024) [1.1]","term":"Composiciones musicales"}
{"id":257,"lang":"es","text":"pues efectivamente descansan sobre las relaciones y proporciones de los intervalos, tanto en su parte melódica como en la armónica.","cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.15])","en_tr":"Ultimately, these laws rest on intervallic relations and proportions in both their melodic and harmonic aspects.","en_cite":"(Cannon-Brown (2024) [2.15])","term":"Intervalo"}
{"id":258,"lang":"pt","text":"Este afastamento da melodia bossa nova para extensões mais restritas e estreitas ajuda-a a se despir das qualidades melodramáticas do samba-canção das décadas anteriores.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The move in bossa nova melodies toward more restricted and narrow melodic range helped to strip away the melodramatic qualities of the samba canção of previous decades.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.10])","term":"extensões"}
{"id":259,"lang":"pt","text":"Rodney Gallop, no seu admirável estudo sobre o Fado (380, abril de 1933 p. 208 e 209) estudando a rítmica do Fado (que aliás considera melhor em 4/4) cita justo um caso de síncopa no primeiro tempo que é tipicamente uma habanera americana, ida naturalmente por intermédio do Brasil. E reconhece outras cantigas portuguesas no mesmo ritmo citadas por Fernandes Tomás (\"Velhas Canções e Romances\") como originárias do Brasil negróide.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 23]","en_tr":"Rodney Gallop, in his admirable study on Fado, studying the rhythm of Fado (which he actually considers better in 4/4), cites precisely a case of syncopation on the first beat, which is typically an American habanera, naturally brought through Brazil. And he recognizes other Portuguese songs in the same rhythm mentioned by Fernandes Tomás (\"Velhas Canções e Romances\") as originating from black Brazil.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) '[1.10]","term":"cantigas"}
{"id":260,"lang":"pt","text":"Como explica Simha Aaron no seu trabalho sobre poliritmia na Africa central (1994), não há um padrão regular nem níveis intermediários (como compassos e tempos fortes) entre a pulsação e o período musical. Este período, formado muitas vezes pela adição de padrões rítmicos de tamanho variado pode ser externalizado através de palmas que marcam os passos da dança ou por um instrumento-guia que toca o que se conhece como \"time-line\".","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"As Simha Arom explains in his work on polyrhythm in Central Africa (1994), there is no regular pattern or intermediate level (such as measures and downbeats) between the pulse level and the musical period. This period, often formed by the addition of rhythmic patterns of varying size, can be externalized through claps that mark the dance steps or by a guide instrument that plays what is known as a time-line.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [4.4])","term":"período"}
{"id":261,"lang":"pt","text":"Na canção popular melodia e letra interferem estreitamente uma sobre a outra. Existem elementos na letra, especialmente sua qualidade narrativa ou lírica que conduzem a diferentes tipos de melodia; existem particularidades na melodia, especialmente seu contorno melódico e tipos de intervalos empregados que marcam o caráter da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In popular song, melody and lyrics closely influence each other. There are elements in the lyrics, especially their narrative or lyrical quality, that suggest different types of melody, and there are particularities in the melody, especially its melodic contour and the types of intervals used that define the character of the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.8])","term":"contorno melódico"}
{"id":262,"lang":"pt","text":"Um dos parâmetros musicais mais discutidos por Mário no Ensaio Sobre a Música Brasileira, e um ponto chave que permeia toda sua obra é a questão do rítmo.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"One of the musical parameters most discussed by Mário de Andrade in Ensaio sobre a músical brasileira, and a key point that permeates his entire work, is the issue of rhythm.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.1])","term":"parâmetros musicais"}
{"id":263,"lang":"pt","text":"A canção popular é um canto acompanhado. A interferência do ritmo da palavra falada na organização temporal, não traz nenhum problema para o canto religioso monódico, mas se torna um elemento complicador para a performance da canção, exatamente por dificultar a sincronização entre a melodia e o acompanhamento.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"A popular song is accompanied singing. The interference in the rhythm of the spoken word's temporal organization does not pose any problem for monodic singing, but it becomes a complicating element for the performance of a song, precisely because it makes synchronization between the melody and the accompaniment difficult.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [4.1])","term":"canção popular"}
{"id":264,"lang":"pt","text":"A prosódia brasileira é silábica, os versos sendo especificados pelo seu número de sílabas (de uma a doze, geralmente, contadas até a última sílaba acentuada); cada tipo de verso tem um número fixo de sílabas, limitados por um acento tônico final obrigatório.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Brazilian prosody is syllabic, verses being specified by their number of syllables (from one to twelve, generally, counted up to the last accented syllable); each type of verse has a fixed number of syllables, limited by an obligatory final tonic accent.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.3])","term":"silábica"}
{"id":265,"lang":"pt","text":"Para existir a síncopa é necessário, portanto, a presença de uma estrutura de compassos com os tempos hierarquicamente colocados para que esta configuração de poder da métrica possa ser desafiada pelo deslocamento dos tempos fortes.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"For there to be syncopation, the presence of metric structure is necessary, with the beats hierarchically arranged so that the configuration of metric strength can be challenged by the displacement of the strong beats.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.3])","term":"métrica possa"}
{"id":266,"lang":"pt","text":"Um dos parâmetros musicais mais discutidos por Mário no Ensaio Sobre a Música Brasileira, e um ponto chave que permeia toda sua obra é a questão do rítmo.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"One of the musical parameters most discussed by Mário de Andrade in Ensaio sobre a músical brasileira, and a key point that permeates his entire work, is the issue of rhythm.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.1])","term":"rítmo"}
{"id":267,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música brasileira ocorreria um conflito entre o processo de concepção rítmica europeia tradicional, que buscaria a simultaneidade de um tempo linear e a a concepção de um tempo circular ameríndio e africano.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In Brazilian music, there is a conflict between temporal process in the traditional European rhythmic conception, which would seek the simultaneity of linear time, and Amerindian and African concepts of circular time.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.5])","term":"tempo circular"}
{"id":268,"lang":"pt","text":"Para existir a síncopa é necessário, portanto, a presença de uma estrutura de compassos com os tempos hierarquicamente colocados para que esta configuração de poder da métrica possa ser desafiada pelo deslocamento dos tempos fortes.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"For there to be syncopation, the presence of metric structure is necessary, with the beats hierarchically arranged so that the configuration of metric strength can be challenged by the displacement of the strong beats.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.3])","term":"estrutura de compassos "}
{"id":269,"lang":"pt","text":"Na concepção brasileira da canção, a melodia é o ponto de partida para a composição, sendo o acompanhamento rítmico e harmônico elementos de suporte melódico. A harmonia, nesta concepção, amplia as possibilidades expressivas do canto melódico podendo os instrumentos acompanhantes criar outras melodias em contraponto à melodia principal, respondendo ou contrapondo-se a ela.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In the Brazilian conception of song, the melody is the starting point for the composition, with the rhythmic and harmonic accompaniment acting as elements of melodic support. Harmony, in this conception, expands the expressive possibilities of melodic singing, with the accompanying instruments able to create other melodies in counterpoint to the main melody, responding to or opposing it.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.7])","term":"harmonia"}
{"id":270,"lang":"pt","text":"Na concepção brasileira da canção, a melodia é o ponto de partida para a composição, sendo o acompanhamento rítmico e harmônico elementos de suporte melódico. A harmonia, nesta concepção, amplia as possibilidades expressivas do canto melódico podendo os instrumentos acompanhantes criar outras melodias em contraponto à melodia principal, respondendo ou contrapondo-se a ela.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In the Brazilian conception of song, the melody is the starting point for the composition, with the rhythmic and harmonic accompaniment acting as elements of melodic support. Harmony, in this conception, expands the expressive possibilities of melodic singing, with the accompanying instruments able to create other melodies in counterpoint to the main melody, responding to or opposing it.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.7])","term":"composição"}
{"id":271,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música de tradição européia clássico-romântica, a articulação da frase pode ser inferida na partitura escrita, pelo menos nos seus aspectos mais óbvios, como duração, colocação métrica, ritmo harmônico, cadências, direção melódica, etc. Entretanto, muito do significado musical só emerge durante o momento da performance. Na performance, e, principalmente no caso da canção popular, cantores usam sua habilidade interpretativa para articular e salientar o conteúdo emocional de cada canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In music of the classical-romantic European tradition, the articulation of the phrase can be inferred from the written score, at least in its most obvious aspects, such as duration, metric placement, harmonic rhythm, cadences, melodic direction, and so on. However, much of the musical meaning only emerges during the moment of performance. In performance, and especially in the case of popular song, singers use their interpretative skills to articulate and highlight the emotional content of each song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.11])","term":"performance"}
{"id":272,"lang":"pt","text":"A ênfase na melodia é tão marcante que todas as notas que a compõem são essenciais para a identidade da canção, incluindo aquelas que seria consideradas ornamentos superficiais na música clássico-romântica européia que tanto influenciou a música brasileira popular. O que poderia ser considerado supérfluo para a avaliação melódica, como notas extranhas à estrutura harmônica básica na canção (grupetos, mordentes, appoggiaturas) têm uma importância funcional na canção brasileira popular.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The emphasis on the melody is so striking that all the notes that compose it are essential to the song's identity, including those that would be considered surface-level ornaments in the European classical-romantic music that has so influenced popular Brazilian music. What could be considered superfluous for melodic evaluation, such as notes that are foreign to the basic harmonic structure of the song (grupetos, mordants, appoggiaturas) have a functional importance in popular Brazilian song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.7])","term":"identidade"}
{"id":273,"lang":"pt","text":"As síncopas europeias, desenvolvidas pelo afro-americano, nos deram o principal da prodigiosa riqueza rítmica que em nossa música se manifesta. Ao contato da polca europeia, que teve entre nós grande aceitação no Segundo Império, os negros brasileiros, da mesma forma com que os negros escravos da Colônia nos tinham dado o samba, nos deram o maxixe, nossa principal dansa de caráter urbano.","cite":"Andrade (2013)","en_tr":"The European syncopations, developed by African-Americans, gave us the main source of the prodigious rhythmic richness that manifests in our music. In contact with the European polka, which had great acceptance in the Second Empire, Brazilian blacks, in the same way that the enslaved blacks of the Colony had given us the samba, gave us the maxixe, our main urban dance.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.4]","term":"maxixe"}
{"id":274,"lang":"pt","text":"Para existir a síncopa é necessário, portanto, a presença de uma estrutura de compassos com os tempos hierarquicamente colocados para que esta configuração de poder da métrica possa ser desafiada pelo deslocamento dos tempos fortes.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"For there to be syncopation, the presence of metric structure is necessary, with the beats hierarchically arranged so that the configuration of metric strength can be challenged by the displacement of the strong beats.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.3])","term":"deslocamento"}
{"id":275,"lang":"pt","text":"No Brasil, a performance musical seria influenciada principalmente pela maneira de acentuar as palavras na fala, cujos \"valores prosódicos … transfiguram a melodia\" (p. 23).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In Brazil, a musical performance is influenced primarily by one's manner of accentuating words in speech, whose \"prosodic values transfigure the melody\" (Andrade 1972, 23).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.1])","term":"accentuar"}
{"id":276,"lang":"pt","text":"As melodias das canções não seriam sincopadas, a ambivalência emergindo da contraposição com o acompanhamento, que acentuaria o tempo. O fluir da melodia seria não-métrico, a acentuação sendo dirigida por uma \"fantasia musical, puro virtuosismo, ou precisão prosódica ... um compromisso sutil entre o canto recitativo e estrófico\" (p. 36).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Song melodies would not be syncopated, the ambivalence emerging from their counterposition with the accompaniment, which would accentuate the beat. Instead, the melodic flow would be non-metrical, its accentuation driven by a \"musical fantasy, pure virtuosity, or prosodic precision … a subtle compromise between recitative and strophic singing\" (36).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.6])","term":"accentuar"}
{"id":277,"lang":"pt","text":"A síncopa europeia me parece um produto exclusivamente musical, e ainda mais, uma verdadeira especulação teórica proveniente da subdivisão da unidade de tempo em quantidades irregulares em que as batidas fortes subsistem em seus lugares teóricos e se tornam pois musicalmente elípticas.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota. no. 9]","en_tr":"European syncopation seems to me an exclusively musical product, and furthermore, a true theoretical speculation stemming from the subdivision of the time unit into irregular quantities where strong beats persist in their theoretical places and thus become musically elliptical.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"subdivisão"}
{"id":278,"lang":"pt","text":"No nº 26, p. 343 vem um Danzon cubano com antecipações. Notar na mesma peça (3ª parte) o grande caráter de peça afroianque mostrando influência de Cuba no jazz.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 28]","en_tr":"In number 26, p. 343, there is a Cuban Danzón with anticipations. Note in the same piece (3rd part) the strong Afro-Cuban character showing influence from Cuba on jazz.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.11]","term":"antecipação"}
{"id":279,"lang":"pt","text":"Estes gestos retóricos, bem como os espaços entre os ataques ou finais de nota dos músicos numa performance musical contribuem enormemente para fazer as pessoas moverem seus corpos de maneira específica, e para escutar o \"grão\" da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"These rhetorical gestures, as well as the spaces between musicians' attacks or note endings in a musical performance, contribute greatly to making people move their bodies in specific ways and to hearing the \"grain\" of the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.8])","term":"finais"}
{"id":280,"lang":"pt","text":"Esta autonomia da melodia aparece com grande frequência na tradição de canção romântica no que chamo de canções tipo modinha. Na performance de modinhas o solo vocal se sobressae à frente do arranjo, com o acompanhamento harmônico instrumental espalhando uma estrutura conhecida e previsível, um leito para o desvelamento de melodias líricas e onduladas.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"This autonomy of melody appears very frequently in the romantic song tradition that I call modinha-type songs. In the performance of modinhas, the vocal solo stands out in front of the arrangement, with the instrumental harmonic accompaniment laying out a known and predictable structure, a bed for the unveiling of lyrical and undulating melodies.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.8])","term":"modinha"}
{"id":281,"lang":"pt","text":"O português brasileiro, como muitas outras línguas, usa o acento silábico como um meio de identificação fonológica. Uma das características principais de seu padrão de acentuação é a presença de um número grande de palavras paroxítonas. Isto dá à língua, e consequentemente ao paradigma musical para estruturação métrica/prosódica uma tendência ou sensação anacrústica.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Brazilian Portuguese, like many other languages, uses syllabic stress as a means of phonological identification. One of the main characteristics of its accentuation patterning is the presence of a large number of paroxytonic words. This gives the language, and consequently the metric/prosodic structuring of its musical paradigm, an anacrustic tendency or feel.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.1])","term":"acento silábico"}
{"id":282,"lang":"pt","text":"Em \"Canção da América\" as palavras expandidas por saltos com ou sem portamento, melisma, tremolo, appoggiaturas as mais diversas, mordentes e grupetos, realçam o conteúdo emocional da canção: o coração chora pela partida - o sentimento preso no peito - e para reestabelecer os laços de amizade tem-se que ouvir o coração, não importa o que aconteça. (p. 325-10).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In \"Canção da América,\" the words expand by leaps with or without portamento, melisma, tremolo, the most diverse appoggiaturas, mordents and grupetos, highlighting the emotional content of the song: the heart cries for escape—the feeling trapped in the chest—and to reestablish the bonds of friendship you have to listen to your heart, no matter what happens. (Carvalho 1990, 325–30).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.7])","term":"tremolo"}
{"id":283,"lang":"pt","text":"Um estudo completo da prosodia musical - incluindo entonação, acento, melodia, ritmo e práticas interpretativas específicas - foge aos limites deste estudo, que se limita a discutir melodia, melodia e língua falada e a relação melodia e acompanhamento na canção brasileira popular.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"A complete study of musical prosody—including intonation, accent, melody, rhythm, and specific interpretative practices—is beyond the limits of this article, which is limited to discussing melody, melody and spoken language, and the relationship between melody and accompaniment in Brazilian popular song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.8])","term":"interpretativas"}
{"id":284,"lang":"pt","text":"Entretanto, muito do significado musical só emerge durante o momento da performance. Na performance, e, principalmente no caso da canção popular, cantores usam sua habilidade interpretativa para articular e salientar o conteúdo emocional de cada canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"However, much of the musical meaning only emerges during the moment of performance. In performance, and especially in the case of popular song, singers use their interpretive skills to articulate and highlight the emotional content of each song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.11])","term":"interpretativas"}
{"id":285,"lang":"pt","text":"Um dos princípios básicos da concepção rítmica europeia, em processo de estruturação na época do achamento do Brasil, como diria Manuel Veiga, é a concepção de compasso, ou verticalização métrica da estrutura musical.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"One of the basic principles of European rhythmic construction, which was in the process of being developed at the time of the discovery of Brazil, as Manuel Veiga would say, is the concept of meter (compasso), or the metric verticalization of musical structure.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.2])","term":"concepção rítmica europeia"}
{"id":286,"lang":"pt","text":"É uma realização imediata e espontânea das nossas maneiras de dançar, mais sensuais, provindas do clima talvez, e do amolecimento fisiológico das raças que se caldearam pra nos formar e formaram também o remeleixo, o requebro, o dengue. É o movimento dengoso do corpo na dança que deformou a rítmica da polca primeiramente na rítmica da habanera em seguida no do maxixe. Acresce ainda que em habaneras e danzones é comum o elemento da tercina (ver se a tercina ocorre no primeiro tempo).","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 9]","en_tr":"Here, syncopation is of immediate, constant, and directly choreographic application. In America, syncopation does not come from European syncopation. It is an immediate and spontaneous realization of our ways of dancing, more sensual, perhaps stemming from the climate, and the physiological softening of the races that melded to form us and also formed the remeleixo, the requebro, the dengue. It is the languid body movement in dance that deformed the rhythm of the polka first into the rhythm of the habanera and then into that of the maxixe. Furthermore, in habaneras and danzones, the element of triplet (check if the triplet occurs on the first beat) is common.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"danzones"}
{"id":287,"lang":"pt","text":"Entretanto, com a bossa nova houve um deslocamento estético nesta relação entre melodia e harmonia na canção. Antes da \"revolução\" bossanovista a harmonia funcionava principalmente como suporte para uma melodia relativamente autônoma. O aparecimento da bossa nova, com sua ênfase num estilo \"parlando\" e canto coloquial, bem como seu uso de progressões harmônicas complexas, representou uma ruptura com o estilo romântico mais antigo. Nos anos sessenta, a expressão melodramática tornara-se cliché. Bossa nova privilegiava uma dicção mais \"cool\" e contida com intenções artísticas e literárias.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"However, with bossa nova, there was an aesthetic shift in the relationship between melody and harmony. Before the bossa nova \"revolution,\" harmony functioned mainly as support for a relatively autonomous melody. The emergence of bossa nova, with its emphasis on a \"parlando\" style and colloquial singing, as well as its use of complex harmonic progressions, represented a break with the romantic style of the time, which had become cliché. Bossa nova favored a cool and more restrained diction, with artistic and literary intentions.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.9])","term":"parlando"}
{"id":288,"lang":"pt","text":"Neste texto amplio alguns aspectos levantados por Mário de Andrade, colocando para discussão uma hipótese sobre a prosódia musical da canção brasileira popular, o conceito de métrica derramada, que se refere tanto a aspectos de sincronização entre canto e acompanhamento como a questões de acentuação na canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In this text I expand on some aspects raised by Andrade, putting up for discussion a hypothesis about musical prosody in Brazilian popular song, the concept of fluid meter [métrica derramada], which refers both to aspects of synchronization between singing and accompaniment and to issues of accentuation in the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.7])","term":"sincronização"}
{"id":289,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música medida de tradição européia todas as partes tendem a se sincronizar precisamente; o tempo é contado em pulsações regulares, geralmente contidos em compassos binários ou ternários, cujos limites são representados por barras de compasso, com uma acentuação no começo de cada compasso.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In metric music of the European tradition, all parts tend to synchronize precisely; time is counted in regular pulsations, generally contained within binary or ternary measures, whose limits are represented by barlines, with an accent at the beginning of each measure.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.12])","term":"sincronização"}
{"id":290,"lang":"pt","text":"Embora cada palavra possa ter suas sílabas tônicas e átonas, é a lógica da sentença que prevalece. Dependendo da sua localização num verso ou frase, uma palavra ou sílaba acentuada pode ter seu acento negligenciado, ou variar em termos de limites silábicos, podendo inclusive as sílabas serem prosódicas ou métricas, como na palavra luar, que pode ser contada como palavra monossilábica, como luar, ou dissílaba, como lu-ar (Carvalho 1970).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Although each word may have its stressed and unstressed syllables, it is the logic of the sentence that prevails. Depending on its location in a verse or phrase, an accented word or syllable may have its accent nullified, or the phrase may vary in terms of syllable limits, and its syllables may even be prosodic or metric, as in the word luar, which can be counted as a monosyllabic word, like \"luar,\" or two-syllable, like \"lu-ar\" (Carvalho 1970).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.3])","term":"tônicas"}
{"id":291,"lang":"pt","text":"Entretanto, com a bossa nova houve um deslocamento estético nesta relação entre melodia e harmonia na canção. Antes da \"revolução\" bossanovista a harmonia funcionava principalmente como suporte para uma melodia relativamente autônoma. O aparecimento da bossa nova, com sua ênfase num estilo \"parlando\" e canto coloquial, bem como seu uso de progressões harmônicas complexas, representou uma ruptura com o estilo romântico mais antigo. Nos anos sessenta, a expressão melodramática tornara-se cliché. Bossa nova privilegiava uma dicção mais \"cool\" e contida com intenções artísticas e literárias.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"However, with bossa nova, there was an aesthetic shift in the relationship between melody and harmony. Before the bossa nova \"revolution,\" harmony functioned mainly as support for a relatively autonomous melody. The emergence of bossa nova, with its emphasis on a \"parlando\" style and colloquial singing, as well as its use of complex harmonic progressions, represented a break with the romantic style of the time, which had become cliché. Bossa nova favored a cool and more restrained diction, with artistic and literary intentions.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.9])","term":"bossa nova"}
{"id":292,"lang":"pt","text":"A melodia da canção popular é geralmente composta a partir da repetição ou agrupamento de motivos melódicos curtos, espécie de fórmulas melódico-rítmicas que funcionam como \"blocos de significação\", como coloca Gino Stefani, prontos para serem incorporados, repetidos, combinados ou associados na feitura da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The melody of a popular song is generally composed of the repetition or grouping of short melodic motifs: melodic-rhythmic formulas that function as \"blocks of meaning,\" as Gino Stefani (1987) puts it, ready to be incorporated, repeated, combined, or associated in creating the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.1])","term":"motivos"}
{"id":293,"lang":"pt","text":"Na infinita maioria dos casos ocorre dentro do conceito de lied. É na canção, e principalmente na canção exclusivamente instrumental (o que é importante para esta observação) que ocorre síncopas. (dar exemplos). [Estudar os flamengos e os ante-monteverdianos pra ver a síncopa neles].","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 9]","en_tr":"In the vast majority of cases, it occurs within the concept of lied. It is in the song, and mainly in the exclusively instrumental song (which is important for this observation), that syncopations occur. (Studying the Flemish and pre-Monteverdian to see the syncopation in them).","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"lied"}
{"id":294,"lang":"pt","text":"A síncopa europeia me parece um produto exclusivamente musical, e ainda mais, uma verdadeira especulação teórica proveniente da subdivisão da unidade de tempo em quantidades irregulares em que as batidas fortes subsistem em seus lugares teóricos e se tornam pois musicalmente elípticas.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota. no. 9]","en_tr":"European syncopation seems to me an exclusively musical product, and furthermore, a true theoretical speculation stemming from the subdivision of the time unit into irregular quantities where strong beats persist in their theoretical places and thus become musically elliptical.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"batidas fortes"}
{"id":295,"lang":"pt","text":"A escanção, ou separação e contagem de sílabas vai depender do número total de sílabas do verso.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The scansion, or separation and counting of syllables, will depend on the total number of syllables in the verse.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.3])","term":"escanção"}
{"id":296,"lang":"pt","text":"A canção popular é um canto acompanhado. A interferência do ritmo da palavra falada na organização temporal, não traz nenhum problema para o canto religioso monódico, mas se torna um elemento complicador para a performance da canção, exatamente por dificultar a sincronização entre a melodia e o acompanhamento.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"A popular song is accompanied singing. The interference in the rhythm of the spoken word's temporal organization does not pose any problem for monodic singing, but it becomes a complicating element for the performance of a song, precisely because it makes synchronization between the melody and the accompaniment difficult.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [4.1])","term":"canto acompanhado"}
{"id":297,"lang":"pt","text":"A melodia está geralmente associada à voz humana, pensamos nela em termos do som contínuo do canto. O canto por sua vez utiliza a linguagem verbal, cujos componentes mínimos são as vogais e consoantes. Um canto feito somente com vogais, entoadas numa linha melódica contínua produz uma melodia no seu estado mais próximo da sensibilidade humana.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Melody is generally associated with the human voice; we think of it in terms of the continuous sound of singing. Singing, in turn, uses verbal language, whose minimum components are vowels and consonants. A song made only with vowels intoned in a continuous melodic line produces a melody in its closest state to human expression.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.3])","term":"consoantes"}
{"id":298,"lang":"pt","text":"Esta pode ser inclusive a razão por que tantas canções brasileiras populares têm uma introdução instrumental: para dar ao cantor ou cantora o tom da música e permitír-lhe começar em anacruse.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"This may even be the reason why so many popular Brazilian songs have an instrumental introduction: to give the singer the tonality of the song and allow them to start with an anacrusis.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.3])","term":"tom"}
{"id":299,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música medida tonal, embora a dinâmica tenha um papel central, duração e freqüência (tanto em classe de altura quanto harmonia) também contribuem para a acentuação musical.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In measured tonal music, although dynamics play a central role, duration and frequency (both in pitch class and harmony) also contribute to musical accentuation.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.10])","term":"freqüência"}
{"id":300,"lang":"pt","text":"A canção popular é um canto acompanhado. A interferência do ritmo da palavra falada na organização temporal, não traz nenhum problema para o canto religioso monódico, mas se torna um elemento complicador para a performance da canção, exatamente por dificultar a sincronização entre a melodia e o acompanhamento.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"A popular song is accompanied singing. The interference in the rhythm of the spoken word's temporal organization does not pose any problem for monodic singing, but it becomes a complicating element for the performance of a song, precisely because it makes synchronization between the melody and the accompaniment difficult.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [4.1])","term":"canto monódico"}
{"id":301,"lang":"pt","text":"A tensão, que Tatit chamaria de tensividade passional, é intensificada pela \"discrepância participativa\" entre solo e acompanhamento.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The intensity, which Tatit would call passionate tenseness, is intensified by the \"participatory discrepancy\" between solo and accompaniment.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.6])","term":"discrepância participativa"}
{"id":302,"lang":"pt","text":"Neste texto amplio alguns aspectos levantados por Mário de Andrade, colocando para discussão uma hipótese sobre a prosódia musical da canção brasileira popular, o conceito de métrica derramada, que se refere tanto a aspectos de sincronização entre canto e acompanhamento como a questões de acentuação na canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In this text I expand on some aspects raised by Andrade, putting up for discussion a hypothesis about musical prosody in Brazilian popular song, the concept of fluid meter [métrica derramada], which refers both to aspects of synchronization between singing and accompaniment and to issues of accentuation in the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.7])","term":"prosódia"}
{"id":303,"lang":"pt","text":"Neste texto amplio alguns aspectos levantados por Mário de Andrade, colocando para discussão uma hipótese sobre a prosódia musical da canção brasileira popular, o conceito de métrica derramada, que se refere tanto a aspectos de sincronização entre canto e acompanhamento como a questões de acentuação na canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In this text I expand on some aspects raised by Andrade, putting up for discussion a hypothesis about musical prosody in Brazilian popular song, the concept of fluid meter [métrica derramada], which refers both to aspects of synchronization between singing and accompaniment and to issues of accentuation in the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.7])","term":"canção brasileira popular"}
{"id":304,"lang":"pt","text":"Luiz Tatit no seu trabalho sobre a canção discute bem o papel das vogais e consoantes na canção. Segundo Tatit (1986, 1996), as vogais são responsáveis pelo que chama de \"tensividade passional\", produzida tanto pela estabilização da curva melódica quanto pela entoação discursiva da fala. Num outro processo de tensividade, agora \"somática\" ou \"temática\", as consoantes geram movimentos, delineiam rítmos, constroem personagens, estabelecem gêneros.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Luiz Tatit, in his work on song, discusses in detail the role vowels and consonants play in the song. According to Tatit (1996), vowels are responsible for what he calls \"passionate tensivity\" [tensividade passional], produced both by the stabilization of the melodic curve and by the discursive intonation of speech. In another process of tensividade, which he describes as \"somatic\" or \"thematic,\" consonants generate movements, outline rhythms, build characters, establish genres.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.6])","term":"somática/temática"}
{"id":305,"lang":"pt","text":"O exemplo mais evidente deste \"derramamento\" é o samba onde se tem um compasso binário, mas com a acentuação transferida do início do compasso para a sua segunda metade.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The most obvious example of this \"overflow\" [derramamento] is samba, where there is a binary measure, but with the accent transferred from the beginning of the measure to its second half.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [4.5])","term":"samba"}
{"id":306,"lang":"pt","text":"O brasileiro fez desta ambivalência \"um elemento de expressão musical\" (p. 32), sendo que muito do que é chamado de sincopado na realidade não seria síncopa na concepção tradicional do termo, mas sim \"rítmos de quem aceita as determinações fisiológicas de arsis e tesis, porem ignora (ou infringe propositalmente) a doutrina dinâmica falsa do compasso\" (pp. 33-34).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The Brazilian musician makes this ambivalence \"an element of musical expression\" (32), and much of what is called syncopation in reality would not be syncopation in the traditional usage of the term, but rather \"rhythms that accept the physiological determinations of arsis and thesis, but ignore (or purposefully infringe on) the false dynamic doctrine of [Western European] meter\" (33–34).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.6])","term":"ambivalência"}
{"id":307,"lang":"pt","text":"Essa \"rítmica oratória\", livre da noção de sucessão previsível de compassos entraria em conflito com os processos rítmicos tradicionais europeus, que funcionam numa estrutura métrica concebida como possuíndo um sentido musical autônomo.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"This \"rhythmic oratory,\" free from the notion of the predictable succession of measures, conflicts with traditional European rhythmic processes, which operate within a metric structure conceived as having an autonomous musical sense.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.5])","term":"rítmica oratória"}
{"id":308,"lang":"pt","text":"A melodia está geralmente associada à voz humana, pensamos nela em termos do som contínuo do canto. O canto por sua vez utiliza a linguagem verbal, cujos componentes mínimos são as vogais e consoantes. Um canto feito somente com vogais, entoadas numa linha melódica contínua produz uma melodia no seu estado mais próximo da sensibilidade humana.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Melody is generally associated with the human voice; we think of it in terms of the continuous sound of singing. Singing, in turn, uses verbal language, whose minimum components are vowels and consonants. A song made only with vowels intoned in a continuous melodic line produces a melody in its closest state to human expression.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.3])","term":"vogais"}
{"id":309,"lang":"pt","text":"Um estudo completo da prosodia musical - incluindo entonação, acento, melodia, ritmo e práticas interpretativas específicas - foge aos limites deste estudo, que se limita a discutir melodia, melodia e língua falada e a relação melodia e acompanhamento na canção brasileira popular.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"A complete study of musical prosody—including intonation, accent, melody, rhythm, and specific interpretative practices—is beyond the limits of this article, which is limited to discussing melody, melody and spoken language, and the relationship between melody and accompaniment in Brazilian popular song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.8])","term":"entonação"}
{"id":310,"lang":"pt","text":"O que é bastante proeminente na música africana, sub-saarana, é o estabelecimento de uma ordem temporal, baseada na interação de partes múltiplas que produzem uma textura polirítmica. A organização rítmica se estrutura a partir de agrupamentos assimétricos de unidades de tempo mínimas ou \"pulso mais rápido\", como explica Kwabena Nketia no seu livro The Music of Africa (1974). Não existe um alinhamento vertical dos inícios dos tempos, como nas noções europeias de compasso.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"What is quite prominent in sub-Saharan African music is the establishment of a temporal order based on the interaction of multiple parts that produce a polyrhythmic texture. The structure of its rhythmic organization is based on asymmetrical groupings of minimum time units or \"fastest pulses,\" as explained by Kwabena Nketia in The Music of Africa (1974). There is no vertical alignment at the beginning of the measure, as in European notions of meter [compasso].","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [4.4])","term":"ordem temporal"}
{"id":311,"lang":"pt","text":"É uma realização imediata e espontânea das nossas maneiras de dançar, mais sensuais, provindas do clima talvez, e do amolecimento fisiológico das raças que se caldearam pra nos formar e formaram também o remeleixo, o requebro, o dengue. É o movimento dengoso do corpo na dança que deformou a rítmica da polca primeiramente na rítmica da habanera em seguida no do maxixe. Acresce ainda que em habaneras e danzones é comum o elemento da tercina (ver se a tercina ocorre no primeiro tempo).","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 9]","en_tr":"Here, syncopation is of immediate, constant, and directly choreographic application. In America, syncopation does not come from European syncopation. It is an immediate and spontaneous realization of our ways of dancing, more sensual, perhaps stemming from the climate, and the physiological softening of the races that melded to form us and also formed the remeleixo, the requebro, the dengue. It is the languid body movement in dance that deformed the rhythm of the polka first into the rhythm of the habanera and then into that of the maxixe. Furthermore, in habaneras and danzones, the element of triplet (check if the triplet occurs on the first beat) is common.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"tercina"}
{"id":312,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música de tradição européia clássico-romântica, a articulação da frase pode ser inferida na partitura escrita, pelo menos nos seus aspectos mais óbvios, como duração, colocação métrica, ritmo harmônico, cadências, direção melódica, etc. Entretanto, muito do significado musical só emerge durante o momento da performance. Na performance, e, principalmente no caso da canção popular, cantores usam sua habilidade interpretativa para articular e salientar o conteúdo emocional de cada canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In music of the classical-romantic European tradition, the articulation of the phrase can be inferred from the written score, at least in its most obvious aspects, such as duration, metric placement, harmonic rhythm, cadences, melodic direction, and so on. However, much of the musical meaning only emerges during the moment of performance. In performance, and especially in the case of popular song, singers use their interpretative skills to articulate and highlight the emotional content of each song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.11])","term":"significado musical "}
{"id":313,"lang":"pt","text":"As melodias das canções não seriam sincopadas, a ambivalência emergindo da contraposição com o acompanhamento, que acentuaria o tempo. O fluir da melodia seria não-métrico, a acentuação sendo dirigida por uma \"fantasia musical, puro virtuosismo, ou precisão prosódica ... um compromisso sutil entre o canto recitativo e estrófico\" (p. 36).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Song melodies would not be syncopated, the ambivalence emerging from their counterposition with the accompaniment, which would accentuate the beat. Instead, the melodic flow would be non-metrical, its accentuation driven by a \"musical fantasy, pure virtuosity, or prosodic precision … a subtle compromise between recitative and strophic singing\" (36).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.6])","term":"melodias"}
{"id":314,"lang":"pt","text":"Quando esta ordem aceita como natural é questionada e a frase começa num tempo fraco e se prolonga no tempo forte seguinte se diz que surgiu uma \"síncopa\".","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"When this accepted natural order is questioned and the musical phrase begins on a weak beat and continues onto the next strong beat, it is said that a \"syncopation\" has occurred.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.3])","term":"síncopa"}
{"id":315,"lang":"pt","text":"O conceito escolar de síncopa, como colocado anteriormente, isto é, \"som articulado sobre um tempo fraco ou parte fraca de um tempo, prolongado sobre o tempo forte ou a parte forte do tempo seguinte\" (definição do Aurélio) nem sempre corresponde ao que acontece de fato em situaçoes de performance.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The academic concept of syncopation, that is, \"sound articulated over a weak beat or weak part of a beat, prolonged over the strong beat or strong part of the next beat\" (the definition given by Aurélio) does not always correspond to what actually happens in performance situations.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.4])","term":"síncopa"}
{"id":316,"lang":"pt","text":"Na canção popular melodia e letra interferem estreitamente uma sobre a outra. Existem elementos na letra, especialmente sua qualidade narrativa ou lírica que conduzem a diferentes tipos de melodia; existem particularidades na melodia, especialmente seu contorno melódico e tipos de intervalos empregados que marcam o caráter da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In popular song, melody and lyrics closely influence each other. There are elements in the lyrics, especially their narrative or lyrical quality, that suggest different types of melody, and there are particularities in the melody, especially its melodic contour and the types of intervals used that define the character of the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.8])","term":"intervalos"}
{"id":317,"lang":"pt","text":"A melodia da canção popular é geralmente composta a partir da repetição ou agrupamento de motivos melódicos curtos, espécie de fórmulas melódico-rítmicas que funcionam como \"blocos de significação\", como coloca Gino Stefani, prontos para serem incorporados, repetidos, combinados ou associados na feitura da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The melody of a popular song is generally composed of the repetition or grouping of short melodic motifs: melodic-rhythmic formulas that function as \"blocks of meaning,\" as Gino Stefani (1987) puts it, ready to be incorporated, repeated, combined, or associated in creating the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.1])","term":"repetição"}
{"id":318,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música de tradição européia clássico-romântica, a articulação da frase pode ser inferida na partitura escrita, pelo menos nos seus aspectos mais óbvios, como duração, colocação métrica, ritmo harmônico, cadências, direção melódica, etc. Entretanto, muito do significado musical só emerge durante o momento da performance. Na performance, e, principalmente no caso da canção popular, cantores usam sua habilidade interpretativa para articular e salientar o conteúdo emocional de cada canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In music of the classical-romantic European tradition, the articulation of the phrase can be inferred from the written score, at least in its most obvious aspects, such as duration, metric placement, harmonic rhythm, cadences, melodic direction, and so on. However, much of the musical meaning only emerges during the moment of performance. In performance, and especially in the case of popular song, singers use their interpretative skills to articulate and highlight the emotional content of each song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.11])","term":"cadências"}
{"id":319,"lang":"pt","text":"Mas o que me faz afirmar que a síncopa europeia é uma especulação prática de música erudita é não só a quase inexistência do movimento sincopado na música popular europeia (com exceção de portugas e ciganas {sobre estes ver Lavignac V}) como por ela não ser corrente mesmo na música coreográfica de criação erudita.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 9]","en_tr":"But what makes me assert that European syncopation is a practical speculation of classical music is not only the almost nonexistence of the syncopated movement in European popular music (with the exception of Portuguese and Gypsy (Lavignac 1913)) as it is not common even in the choreographic music of the Western classical tradition.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"música erudita"}
{"id":320,"lang":"pt","text":"A melodia está geralmente associada à voz humana, pensamos nela em termos do som contínuo do canto. O canto por sua vez utiliza a linguagem verbal, cujos componentes mínimos são as vogais e consoantes. Um canto feito somente com vogais, entoadas numa linha melódica contínua produz uma melodia no seu estado mais próximo da sensibilidade humana.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Melody is generally associated with the human voice; we think of it in terms of the continuous sound of singing. Singing, in turn, uses verbal language, whose minimum components are vowels and consonants. A song made only with vowels intoned in a continuous melodic line produces a melody in its closest state to human expression.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.3])","term":"voz"}
{"id":321,"lang":"pt","text":"Ora pois, se nos faltam dados positivos de fórmulas e de datas como estabelecer prioridade de criação e de imposição na América e no Brasil, de certas manifestações rítmicas e melódicas já agora definitivamente nossas?","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 1]","en_tr":"Now then, if we lack positive data on formulas and dates, how can we establish priority of creation and imposition in America and Brazil, of certain rhythmic and melodic manifestations that are now definitively ours?","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"melódicas"}
{"id":322,"lang":"pt","text":"De fato, a bossa nova cumpre no samba urbano o ideal modernista-nacionalista preconizado por Mário: a de tornar \"estético\" o \"funcional\".","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In fact, bossa nova fulfills in urban samba the modernist-nationalist ideal advocated by Andrade: that of making the \"functional\" \"aesthetic.\"","en_cite":"(Stover (2024)[2.10])","term":"funcional"}
{"id":323,"lang":"pt","text":"Em primeiro lugar, melodias populares são \"música cantável\", e em segundo lugar, emergem de uma \"matriz oral\" conectada à voz cantante e a um sentido de prazer primário.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"First of all, popular melodies are \"singable music,\" and second, they emerge from an \"oral matrix\" connected to the singing voice and a primary sense of pleasure.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.1])","term":"matriz oral"}
{"id":324,"lang":"pt","text":"A ênfase na melodia é tão marcante que todas as notas que a compõem são essenciais para a identidade da canção, incluindo aquelas que seria consideradas ornamentos superficiais na música clássico-romântica européia que tanto influenciou a música brasileira popular. O que poderia ser considerado supérfluo para a avaliação melódica, como notas extranhas à estrutura harmônica básica na canção (grupetos, mordentes, appoggiaturas) têm uma importância funcional na canção brasileira popular.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The emphasis on the melody is so striking that all the notes that compose it are essential to the song's identity, including those that would be considered surface-level ornaments in the European classical-romantic music that has so influenced popular Brazilian music. What could be considered superfluous for melodic evaluation, such as notes that are foreign to the basic harmonic structure of the song (grupetos, mordants, appoggiaturas) have a functional importance in popular Brazilian song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.7])","term":"mordentes"}
{"id":325,"lang":"pt","text":"Em \"Canção da América\" as palavras expandidas por saltos com ou sem portamento, melisma, tremolo, appoggiaturas as mais diversas, mordentes e grupetos, realçam o conteúdo emocional da canção: o coração chora pela partida - o sentimento preso no peito - e para reestabelecer os laços de amizade tem-se que ouvir o coração, não importa o que aconteça. (p. 325-10).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In \"Canção da América,\" the words expand by leaps with or without portamento, melisma, tremolo, the most diverse appoggiaturas, mordents and grupetos, highlighting the emotional content of the song: the heart cries for escape—the feeling trapped in the chest—and to reestablish the bonds of friendship you have to listen to your heart, no matter what happens. (Carvalho 1990, 325–30).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.7])","term":"mordentes"}
{"id":326,"lang":"pt","text":"É significativo que tanto a letra quanto a música, no momento de maior \"discrepância\" entre a melodia cantante e o acompanhamento, articulam uma anacruse anunciadora do ponto principal feito pela letra (a rosa do amor tem sempre que crescer/a rosa do amor não vai despetalar/Prá quem cuida bem da rosa/Prá quem sabe cultivar).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"It is significant that both the lyrics and the music, at the moment of major \"discrepancy\" between the sung melody and the accompaniment, articulate an anacrusis announcing the main point made by the lyrics (\"a rosa do amor tem sempre que crescer / a rosa do amor não vai despetalar / Pra quem cuida bem da rosa / Pra quem sabe cultivar\").","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.4])","term":"discrepância"}
{"id":327,"lang":"pt","text":"Na música medida tonal, embora a dinâmica tenha um papel central, duração e freqüência (tanto em classe de altura quanto harmonia) também contribuem para a acentuação musical.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In measured tonal music, although dynamics play a central role, duration and frequency (both in pitch class and harmony) also contribute to musical accentuation.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.10])","term":"duração"}
{"id":328,"lang":"pt","text":"O compasso permite que várias vozes possam apresentar um discurso homogêneo ao propor a organização interna das pulsações em tempos fortes, propulsores de energia e tempos fracos e inerciais.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Meter allows several voices to present a homogeneous (musical) discourse by providing an internal organization of pulsations into strong beats, propelling energy, and weak, inertial beats.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.2])","term":"tempos fortes"}
{"id":329,"lang":"pt","text":"Estes espaços métricos são muito difíceis de demonstrar com a notação ocidental convencional. Etnomusicólogos têm criado sinais para expressar estes ataques \"adiantados\" ou \"atrasados\".","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"These metric spaces are very difficult to illustrate with conventional Western notation. Ethnomusicologists have created signs to express these \"early\" or \"late\" attacks.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.5])","term":"ataques"}
{"id":330,"lang":"pt","text":"De fato, a bossa nova cumpre no samba urbano o ideal modernista-nacionalista preconizado por Mário: a de tornar \"estético\" o \"funcional\".","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In fact, bossa nova fulfills in urban samba the modernist-nationalist ideal advocated by Andrade: that of making the \"functional\" \"aesthetic.\"","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.10])","term":"estético"}
{"id":331,"lang":"pt","text":"As melodias das canções não seriam sincopadas, a ambivalência emergindo da contraposição com o acompanhamento, que acentuaria o tempo. O fluir da melodia seria não-métrico, a acentuação sendo dirigida por uma \"fantasia musical, puro virtuosismo, ou precisão prosódica ... um compromisso sutil entre o canto recitativo e estrófico\" (p. 36).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Song melodies would not be syncopated, the ambivalence emerging from their counterposition with the accompaniment, which would accentuate the beat. Instead, the melodic flow would be non-metrical, its accentuation driven by a \"musical fantasy, pure virtuosity, or prosodic precision … a subtle compromise between recitative and strophic singing\" (36).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.6])","term":"canção"}
{"id":332,"lang":"pt","text":"Em primeiro lugar, melodias populares são \"música cantável\", e em segundo lugar, emergem de uma \"matriz oral\" conectada à voz cantante e a um sentido de prazer primário.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"First of all, popular melodies are \"singable music,\" and second, they emerge from an \"oral matrix\" connected to the singing voice and a primary sense of pleasure.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.1])","term":"música cantável"}
{"id":333,"lang":"pt","text":"A síncopa europeia me parece um produto exclusivamente musical, e ainda mais, uma verdadeira especulação teórica proveniente da subdivisão da unidade de tempo em quantidades irregulares em que as batidas fortes subsistem em seus lugares teóricos e se tornam pois musicalmente elípticas.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota. no. 9]","en_tr":"European syncopation seems to me an exclusively musical product, and furthermore, a true theoretical speculation stemming from the subdivision of the time unit into irregular quantities where strong beats persist in their theoretical places and thus become musically elliptical.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"elípticas"}
{"id":334,"lang":"pt","text":"Portanto, na versificação portuguesa, o verso é a medida métrica, enquanto as sílabas, as pulsações mínimas, são combinadas em agrupamentos rítmicos variados. Comparando esta organização métrica da língua falada e a organização métrica musical ocidental e não-ocidental podemos dizer que a prosódia do verso português está mais para uma noção métrica africana sub-saarana (composta de períodos ou \"time lines\" sem acentos recorrentes), que para uma noção métrica européia clássico-romântica (cujos compassos de limites determinados, se sucedem regularmente).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In Portuguese versification, the verse is the metric measure, while the syllables, the minimal pulsations, are combined in varied rhythmic groupings. Comparing this metric organization of spoken language with Western and non-Western musical metric organization, we can say that the prosody of Portuguese verse is more like a sub-Saharan African metric notion (composed of periods or \"time lines\" without recurring accents) than a classical-romantic European metric notion (whose measures of determined limits follow one another regularly [see Example 3.1 - translator's note]).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.4])","term":"medida métrica"}
{"id":335,"lang":"pt","text":"A melodia da canção popular é geralmente composta a partir da repetição ou agrupamento de motivos melódicos curtos, espécie de fórmulas melódico-rítmicas que funcionam como \"blocos de significação\", como coloca Gino Stefani, prontos para serem incorporados, repetidos, combinados ou associados na feitura da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The melody of a popular song is generally composed of the repetition or grouping of short melodic motifs: melodic-rhythmic formulas that function as \"blocks of meaning,\" as Gino Stefani (1987) puts it, ready to be incorporated, repeated, combined, or associated in creating the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.1])","term":"agrupamento"}
{"id":336,"lang":"pt","text":"Embora cada palavra possa ter suas sílabas tônicas e átonas, é a lógica da sentença que prevalece. Dependendo da sua localização num verso ou frase, uma palavra ou sílaba acentuada pode ter seu acento negligenciado, ou variar em termos de limites silábicos, podendo inclusive as sílabas serem prosódicas ou métricas, como na palavra luar, que pode ser contada como palavra monossilábica, como luar, ou dissílaba, como lu-ar (Carvalho 1970).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Although each word may have its stressed and unstressed syllables, it is the logic of the sentence that prevails. Depending on its location in a verse or phrase, an accented word or syllable may have its accent nullified, or the phrase may vary in terms of syllable limits, and its syllables may even be prosodic or metric, as in the word luar, which can be counted as a monosyllabic word, like \"luar,\" or two-syllable, like \"lu-ar\" (Carvalho 1970).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.3])","term":"átonas"}
{"id":337,"lang":"pt","text":"Ora em nossa música americana (jazz, maxixe e em geral toda síncopa brasileira e mesmo no tango platino) o que se dá é um verdadeiro descolocamento do acento forte que passa do lugar teórico para um lugar onde ele não devia cair, verdadeira antecipação rítmica da thesis.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 9]","en_tr":"Now in our American music (jazz, maxixe, and in general all Brazilian syncopation and even in the Argentine tango) what happens is a true displacement of the strong accent which passes from the theoretical place to a place where it should not fall, a true rhythmic anticipation of the thesis.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"thesis"}
{"id":338,"lang":"pt","text":"Esta rítmica se torna tão sutil que é quase impossível registrá-la através da notação tradicional.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The resulting rhythm becomes so subtle that it is almost impossible to register it through traditional notation.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.1])","term":"notação tradicional"}
{"id":339,"lang":"pt","text":"Na canção popular melodia e letra interferem estreitamente uma sobre a outra. Existem elementos na letra, especialmente sua qualidade narrativa ou lírica que conduzem a diferentes tipos de melodia; existem particularidades na melodia, especialmente seu contorno melódico e tipos de intervalos empregados que marcam o caráter da canção.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In popular song, melody and lyrics closely influence each other. There are elements in the lyrics, especially their narrative or lyrical quality, that suggest different types of melody, and there are particularities in the melody, especially its melodic contour and the types of intervals used that define the character of the song.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [1.8])","term":"letra"}
{"id":340,"lang":"pt","text":"Tanto nestas \"melôs\", quanto no caso do rap em português vão aparecer duas questões prosódicas: primeiro, a utilização no português de uma métrica própria do ingles, isto é, de acentuações téticas regularmente espaçadas, o que contribui para uma sensação de compassos regulares. Segundo, é a questão das rupturas sucessivas próprias do rap, produzidas pelos \"scratchs\", o que faz da música mais uma \"parceria rítmica\" do que um todo interligado de letra e melodia (vide Rose 1997: 207-8).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Both in these \"melôs\" and in the case of rap in Portuguese, two prosodic issues appear. First is the use in Portuguese of a metric typical of English, that is, of regularly spaced thetic accents, which contributes to a sensation of regular measures. And second, there is the issue of successive ruptures typical of rap, produced by scratches, which makes music more of a \"rhythmic partnership\" than an complete interconnection between lyrics and melody (see Rose 1997, 207–8).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.5])","term":"parceria rítmica"}
{"id":341,"lang":"pt","text":"Luiz Tatit no seu trabalho sobre a canção discute bem o papel das vogais e consoantes na canção. Segundo Tatit (1986, 1996), as vogais são responsáveis pelo que chama de \"tensividade passional\", produzida tanto pela estabilização da curva melódica quanto pela entoação discursiva da fala. Num outro processo de tensividade, agora \"somática\" ou \"temática\", as consoantes geram movimentos, delineiam rítmos, constroem personagens, estabelecem gêneros.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"Luiz Tatit, in his work on song, discusses in detail the role vowels and consonants play in the song. According to Tatit (1996), vowels are responsible for what he calls \"passionate tensivity\" [tensividade passional], produced both by the stabilization of the melodic curve and by the discursive intonation of speech. In another process of tensividade, which he describes as \"somatic\" or \"thematic,\" consonants generate movements, outline rhythms, build characters, establish genres.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [2.6])","term":"tensividade passional"}
{"id":342,"lang":"pt","text":"A tensão, que Tatit chamaria de tensividade passional, é intensificada pela \"discrepância participativa\" entre solo e acompanhamento.","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"The intensity, which Tatit would call passionate tenseness, is intensified by the \"participatory discrepancy\" between solo and accompaniment.","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [5.6])","term":"tensividade passional"}
{"id":343,"lang":"pt","text":"A contaminação se deu e por ela se criaram fórmulas de cantar já especificamente americanas. Porém esta afirmativa não basta. O problema das origens permanece intrincado e sem bases atuais com que possa ser resolvido.","cite":"Andrade (n.d.) [Nota no. 1]","en_tr":"Contamination occurred and through it formulas of singing were created that are already specifically American. However, this statement is not enough. The problem of origins remains intricate and without current bases on which it can be resolved.","en_cite":"Menezes (2024) [1.5]","term":"cantar"}
{"id":344,"lang":"pt","text":"Portanto, na versificação portuguesa, o verso é a medida métrica, enquanto as sílabas, as pulsações mínimas, são combinadas em agrupamentos rítmicos variados. Comparando esta organização métrica da língua falada e a organização métrica musical ocidental e não-ocidental podemos dizer que a prosódia do verso português está mais para uma noção métrica africana sub-saarana (composta de períodos ou \"time lines\" sem acentos recorrentes), que para uma noção métrica européia clássico-romântica (cujos compassos de limites determinados, se sucedem regularmente).","cite":"(Ulhôa (1999))","en_tr":"In Portuguese versification, the verse is the metric measure, while the syllables, the minimal pulsations, are combined in varied rhythmic groupings. Comparing this metric organization of spoken language with Western and non-Western musical metric organization, we can say that the prosody of Portuguese verse is more like a sub-Saharan African metric notion (composed of periods or \"time lines\" without recurring accents) than a classical-romantic European metric notion (whose measures of determined limits follow one another regularly [see Example 3.1 - translator's note]).","en_cite":"(Stover (2024) [3.4])","term":"versificação"}
